\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 2016\par 12:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Germany's Economic Rebound Flagging, Survey Finds \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German economic sentiment stabilized at a moderate level in September, a sign that Europe's largest economy has lost some momentum after a strong start to the year. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par British Firms Face Higher Costs After Brexit \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A fall in sterling since the U.K. voted to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  pushed up British firms' raw material costs in August at the fastest annual pace in almost five years. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China's Economy Rebounds \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A slew of data points reported Tuesday-from factory output to retail sales-showed rebounding economic activity in August after a wobbly few months, economists said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IEA Cuts Global Oil Demand Forecast \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Energy Agency\f28 \uc2 \f2  sharply cut its forecast for global oil demand for this year and the next amid what it called "wobbling" Asian demand. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Clinton to Release More Medical Records After Pneumonia Diagnosis \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hillary Clinton\f28 \uc2 \f2  will release additional medical records this week, her campaign said Monday, moving to contain concerns about her well-being and forthrightness after she stumbled exiting a 9/11 ceremony. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU Court Rules Crime Insufficient Reason to Deport Single Parents \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  countries aren't allowed to expel from their territory single parents of \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  children just because they have a criminal record, the bloc's top court ruled Tuesday in Luxembourg. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  Steps Up Effort to Cool Bond Market \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  used a longer-dated tool to inject cash into the financial system for the first time in seven months, intensifying its effort to cool the domestic bond market. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Surge in Offshore Yuan Borrowing Rate Suggests \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The most vibrant market for yuan trading outside mainland \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has turned into a key battleground for Beijing to defend the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Trump Claims Yellen Is Holding Rates Low to Aid Obama \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 GOP presidential nominee \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  ratcheted up his criticism of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Chairwoman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2 , saying the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is keeping rates low to help President Obama. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.S. Flies Bombers Over South Korea in Show of Force Against North \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. on Tuesday sent nuclear-capable supersonic bombers streaking over ally South Korea in a show of force meant to cow North Korea after its recent nuclear test and to settle rattled nerves in the South.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 13, 2016 06:02 ET (10:02 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160913ec9d0011k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
