\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Global Markets News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 731 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2016\par 16:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par STOCK SELLOFF RESUMES AMID FEARS OF TIGHTER POLICY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks traded lower Monday amid concerns about tighter monetary policy, extending a rout that halted two months of calm summer trading. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CANADIAN FERTILIZER GIANTS AGRIUM AND POTASH TO MERGE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canadian fertilizer giants \f28 \uc2 \f2 Agrium\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Potash Corp. of Saskatchewan\f28 \uc2 \f2  said they would combine to create one of the largest crop-nutrient companies in the world, with $20.6 billion in annual revenue. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OPEN TEXT\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO BUY DELL EMC ENTERPRISE CONTENT DIVISION \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canadian information-technology provider \f28 \uc2 \f2 Open Text\f28 \uc2 \f2  agreed to buy the enterprise content division of the newly merged \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dell Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 EMC Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for $1.62 billion. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par E*TRADE NAMES NEW CEO IN EXECUTIVE SHAKE-UP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 E*Trade\f28 \uc2 \f2  named General Counsel \f28 \uc2 \f2 Karl Roessner\f28 \uc2 \f2  as chief executive, succeeding Paul Idzik, in a shake up of its executive ranks. Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rodger Lawson\f28 \uc2 \f2  will become executive chairman. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FED'S KASHKARI: NO 'HUGE URGENCY' TO 'DO ANYTHING' \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of Minneapolis President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Neel Kashkari\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Monday said regulatory and fiscal policies at present outweigh monetary policy as the tools needed to spur the economy. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAMSUNG\f28 \uc2 \f2  NOMINATES HEIR APPARENT TO BOARD AS SHARES SLAMMED \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung\f28 \uc2 \f2  nominated Lee Jae-yong, son of its longtime chairman, to the board as its shares suffered their steepest one-day decline since 2008 after the wake of the Galaxy Note 7 recall. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  PROPOSALS AIM TO CLEAR EUROPE'S BAD DEBT MOUNTAIN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  published new proposals aimed at forcing eurozone banks to deal with a $1 trillion mountain of bad debt, which is weighing on bank stocks and hindering the region's economic recovery. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HP\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO ACQUIRE \f28 \uc2 \f2 SAMSUNG\f28 \uc2 \f2  PRINTER BUSINESS IN $1 BILLION DEAL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HP\f28 \uc2 \f2  will buy \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung\f28 \uc2 \f2 's printer business for $1.05 billion, a deal aimed at helping the Silicon Valley company expand into high-volume devices that handle printing and copying for office work groups. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 VALVOLINE\f28 \uc2 \f2  EXPECTS TO RAISE $605 MILLION IN IPO \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Valvoline Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said it plans to sell 30 million shares for between $20 and $23 a share in its initial public offering, raising roughly $605 million in net proceeds as it spins off from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ashland Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . later this year. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 1MDB SCANDAL AROUND MALAYSIA PRIME MINISTER PUTS NEW SPOTLIGHT ON WIFE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Documents show $6 million in credit-card spending drawing renewed scrutiny of Rosmah Mansor, amid allegations that her husband and people close to him siphoned more than $3 billion from a state investment fund, 1MDB. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Election 2016 \par CLINTON'S PNEUMONIA JOLTS THE PRESIDENTIAL RACE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hillary Clinton\f28 \uc2 \f2 's campaign said Sunday she has been diagnosed with pneumonia, the latest jolt in a presidential race that has been tightening. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Election 2016 \par FLORIDA TESTS DIVERGENT STRATEGIES OF CLINTON, TRUMP \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With less than four weeks until Florida officials start mailing ballots to voters, the race in the nation's biggest swing state is shaping up to be a defining test of political enthusiasm versus traditional organization. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Central Banks \par SURGE IN OFFSHORE YUAN BORROWING RATE SUGGESTS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CHINA INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The most vibrant market for yuan trading outside mainland \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has turned into a key battleground for Beijing to defend the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Heard on the Street \par BOND MARKETS JUST WAKING UP TO THEIR OWN CRAZINESS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bond markets are wobbling, but it is the risk-free government-bond market that looks most fragile of all. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par STOCK SELLOFF RESUMES AMID FEARS OF TIGHTER POLICY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks traded lower Monday amid concerns about tighter monetary policy, extending a rout that halted two months of calm summer trading. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par TREASURYS STRENGTHEN FOLLOWING KASHKARI COMMENTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasurys strengthened after dovish comments by Minneapolis Fed President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Neel Kashkari\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DOLLAR FALLS VS YEN, GAINS VS RISKIER \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fell against the yen, was flat against the euro and sterling, and strengthened against commodity-linked and emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par OIL PRICES DROP ON RECEDING HOPES FOR A PRODUCTION FREEZE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil prices pulled back amid receding hopes for a production freeze deal and a broad perception that last week's significant drop in U.S. crude inventories was unlikely to be sustained. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GOLD PRICES FLUCTUATE ON INVESTOR UNCERTAINTY OVER FED RATE TALK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold prices swung between gains and losses on Monday in London, with investors looking for clues about the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's policy moves.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 12, 2016 10:02 ET (14:02 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160912ec9c001uo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
