\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-China August  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves fall to lowest since 2011\b0\par\par\uc2 534 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2016\par 10:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst comment, context)\par \par \uc2 BEIJING, Sept 7 (Reuters) - China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to the lowest since 2011 in August as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it weakened to near-six year lows.\par \par \uc2 While the $15.89 billion drop was in line with market expectations and was described by analysts as modest, it was the biggest decline since May and could signal fresh capital outflows from the economy even as it starts to show signs of steadying.\par \par \uc2 China's reserves fell to $3.185 trillion in August -- the lowest since December 2011 -- from $3.20 trillion at the end of July, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 China's reserves, the largest in the world, fell by a record $513 billion last year after Beijing devalued the yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sparking a flood of capital outflows that threatened to destabilise the world's second-largest economy and alarmed global financial markets.\par \par \uc2 But declines have slowed sharply in recent months as authorities tightened capital controls and cracked down on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading which is suspected to be speculation.\par \par \uc2 Traders believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stepped in via state-run banks since mid-July to slow the pace of depreciation in the yuan, which has weakened 2.6 percent against the U.S. dollar so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Analysts expect pressure on the yuan and reserves to continue as expectations of another \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  interest rate hike this year support the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Lower \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves data is not surprising in light of the active \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen ahead of the G20 meeting (in \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) in early September," said Chester Liaw, an economist at Forecast Pte Ltd in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 "With a Fed rate hike likely before the end of the year, the authorities will have their hands full with containing any wild spikes in USDCNY triggered by capital outflows, and can expect \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to remain on a downward path through to the end of the year."\par \par \uc2 Nie Wen, an economist at Hwabao Trust in Shanghai, said a monthly drop of $10 billion-$20 billion in reserves "should be normal."\par \par \uc2 "The pressure is relatively small compared with last year and large-scale capital outflows should be over... partly because capital controls are stricter than last year."\par \par \uc2 The impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply and demand remains under control, the \uc2 State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SAFE) said recently in a statement, adding that it expected cross-border capital flows to remain stable in the medium- to long-term.\par \par \uc2 Net \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales by the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  jumped to their highest in five months in July, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sought to support the yuan after it briefly broke through the key psychological level of 6.7 to the dollar. On Wednesday it was trading around 6.66.\par \par \uc2 China's gold reserves fell to $77.18 billion at the end of August, down from $78.89 billion at end-July, data on the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  website showed.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kevin Yao, Elias Glenn and the Beijing Monitoring Desk; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-9-7T09:46:30.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160907ec9700e4p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
