\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan weakens, eyes on 6.7/dlr-level as US rate hike talk persists\b0\par\par\uc2 521 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 September 2016\par 06:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI, Sept 6 (Reuters) - China's yuan weakened on Tuesday as speculation that U.S. interest rates will rise by the year end fueled dollar buying despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  setting a stronger mid-point for the the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The yuan firmed slightly in early trade as investors took advantage of a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  midpoint but swiftly reversed course once dollar buyers emerged.\par \par \uc2 "Investors are anxiously seeking clues to whether the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  will raise interest rates in the near term," said a trader at a European bank in Shanghai.\par \par \uc2 "Once the U.S. hike the rates, the yuan may breach the important 6.7 level," he said.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  set the midpoint rate at 6.6676 per dollar prior to market open on Tuesday, firmer than the previous fix 6.6873.\par \par \uc2 Traders believe the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  (PBOC) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stabilise the yuan when it weakened past 6.7 per dollar in mid-July for the first time in more than five years.\par \par \uc2 The spot market opened at 6.6775 per dollar and was changing hands at 6.6816 at midday, 48 pips away from the previous late session close and 0.21 percent away from the midpoint.\par \par \uc2 The Thomson Reuters/HKEX Global CNH index, which tracks the offshore yuan against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a daily basis, stood at 94.84, firmer than the previous day's 94.83.\par \par \uc2 The global dollar index fell to 95.755 from the previous close of 95.844.\par \par \uc2 The offshore yuan was trading 0.13 percent weaker than the onshore spot at 6.6905 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Offshore one-year non-deliverable forwards contracts (NDFs), considered the best available proxy for forward-looking market expectations of the yuan's value, traded at 6.8375, 2.48 percent weaker than the midpoint.\par \par \uc2 One-year NDFs are settled against the midpoint, not the spot rate.\par \par \uc2 The yuan market at 3:37 AM GMT:\par \par \uc2 ONSHORE SPOT: Item Current Previous Change PBOC midpoint 6.6676 6.6873 0.30%\par \par \uc2 Spot yuan 6.6816 6.6768 -0.07%\par \par \uc2 \f2 Divergence from    0.21%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change YTD                       -2.81%\par  Spot change since 2005                23.87%\par  revaluation\par               \par Key indexes:\par  Item            Current     Previous  Change\par               \par Thomson         94.84       94.83     0.0\par  Reuters/HKEX                          \par  CNH index                             \par  Dollar index    95.755      95.844    -0.1\par               \par               \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each morning.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OFFSHORE CNH MARKET Instrument Current Difference\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from onshore \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  Offshore spot yuan    6.6905    -0.13%\par  *                        \par  Offshore              6.8375    -2.48%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par  **                \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 *Premium for offshore spot over onshore **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint, since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint. .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting By Winni Zhou and Nathaniel Taplin; Editing by Simon Cameron-Moore) \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-9-6T05:01:36.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160906ec960066f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
