\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan weakens on global dollar strength, hits record low vs basket\b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 2016\par 06:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Aug 22 (Reuters) - China's yuan weakened on Monday\par as the dollar strengthened globally, while an official index\par showed that it hit a record low against a basket of\par trade-weighted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week.\par     "The yuan weakened inverse to the dollar's global\par performance, while the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stayed on the sidelines,"\par said a trader at a European bank in Shanghai.\par     "As the yuan's performance is largely stable of late, the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has greatly reduced its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in trading."\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set the midpoint rate\par  at 6.6652 per dollar prior to the market open, weaker\par than the previous fix of 6.6211. \par     In the spot market, the yuan opened at 6.6630 per\par dollar and was changing hands at 6.6653 at midday, 107 pips away\par from the previous late session close and in line with the\par midpoint. \par     It has slid 2.5 percent against the dollar so far this year,\par and 6.8 percent against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The latest China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Trade System (CFETS) data\par showed that the index for the yuan's value based on the market's\par trade-weighted basket stood at a new low of 94.11 on\par Friday, toppling the previous mark of 94.25 on July 8.\par     Traders said the move reflected that the market still\par expected the yuan to depreciate in the medium term.\par     "Corporate dollar demand has remained strong despite a\par general yuan rebound since mid-July," said a trader at a Chinese\par commercial bank in Shanghai.\par     "Investors still believe the yuan will depreciate in the\par foreseeable future, given the prospects of the dollar's global\par strengthening and of the slowdown of the growth of the Chinese\par economy."\par     The Thomson Reuters/HKEX Global CNH index, which\par tracks the offshore yuan against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on a\par daily basis, stood at 94.73, firmer than the previous day's\par 94.68. \par     The global dollar index rose to 94.905 from the\par previous close of 94.511. \par     The offshore yuan was trading -0.13 percent away from the\par onshore spot at 6.6738 per dollar. \par     \par     The yuan market at 0422 GMT: \par     \par     ONSHORE SPOT:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  PBOC midpoint      6.6652   6.6211    -0.66%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.6648   6.6546    -0.15%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    -0.01%             \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change YTD                       -2.57%\par  Spot change since 2005                24.18%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par     Key indexes:\par      \par  Item            Current     Previous  Change\par                                        \par  Thomson         94.78       94.68     0.1\par  Reuters/HKEX                          \par  CNH index                             \par  Dollar index    94.883      94.511    0.4\par  \par     \par     \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.6727    -0.12%\par         *                        \par  Offshore              6.8065    -2.08%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     \par \par  \par   \par \par \par \par \par \par     \par \par     \par  (Reporting by Lu Jianxin and Nathaniel Taplin; Editing by Kim\par Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-8-22T05:29:14.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160822ec8m0093t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
