\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  bulls ride on global easy money hopes; yuan views optimistic\b0\par\par\uc2 857 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2016\par 09:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Yuan sentiment bullish, first time in 4 mths on strong fix\par     * Won most optimistic in 2 years on S&P, capital inflows\par     * Taiwan dlr long positions 4-1/2-yr high on equity inflows\par \par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 18 (Reuters) - Optimism prevailed over\par emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the last two weeks with sentiment\par on China's yuan turning bullish, a Reuters poll showed,\par supported by expectations of an extended phase of easy monetary\par policies around the globe. \par     The yuan was estimated to report small bullish\par bets for the first time since mid-April, according to the survey\par of 23 fund managers, analysts and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders conducted\par from Tuesday through Thursday. (GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2aDRP78"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2aDRP78}}}\uc2 \f2 )\par     That came as \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a series of firm daily\par guidance rates in a move to stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par Chinese holdings of U.S. Treasuries also dipped in June.\par  \par     Two weeks ago, bearish bets on the renminbi fell to its\par lowest in more than three months as shown by the previous poll\par published on Aug 4, as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to slow down the pace of its depreciation.\par  Recent dollar weakness has also helped the yuan\par rebound.\par     The dollar came under pressure as the recent disappointing\par U.S. economic data underlined expectations that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal\par Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  will remain cautious on raising interest rates further.\par     The Fed policymakers agreed that more economic data is\par needed before increasing interest rates although some see a need\par to tighten policy soon, the minutes of the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par latest policy meeting showed. \par     Other major central banks are expected to deliver further\par monetary stimulus, helping investors seek higher yields in\par emerging Asia.\par     As a result, most regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reported largest long\par positions in multi years.\par     \par     WON WINS\par     Views around the South Korean won were the most\par optimistic among regional peers with its bullish bets highest\par since July 2014.\par     The positive mood coincided with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  last week\par raising the country's sovereign rating, fuelling capital\par inflows. \par     The Taiwan dollar reported the largest optimistic\par bets since February 2012 on equity inflows. Foreign investors\par bought a combined net T$57.9 billion ($1.8 billion) worth of the\par island's stocks in the first half of this month after posting\par the biggest inflows in a decade in July. \par     Thailand's baht posted the largest bullish bets\par since April 2013 on capital inflows. Adding to the optimism, the\par economy grew at its fastest annual rate in 13 quarters, above\par forecasts. \par     The Indian rupee - one of the highest-yielding\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Asia - saw the largest long positions since March\par 2015.\par     Bullish bets on the Philippine peso grew to the\par largest in near five months.\par     Sentiment on the Malaysian ringgit turned\par optimistic, for the first time since late April, as the country\par saw bond inflows in July despite persistent concerns over\par scandal-plagued state fund \f28 \uc2 \f2 1Malaysia Development Berhad\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The poll is focused on what analysts and fund managers\par believe are the current market positions in nine Asian emerging\par market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : the Chinese yuan, South Korean won, Singapore\par dollar, Indonesian rupiah, Taiwan dollar,\par Indian rupee, Philippine peso, Malaysian ringgit and the Thai\par baht.\par     The poll uses estimates of net long or short positions on a\par scale of minus 3 to plus 3. A score of plus 3 indicates the\par market is significantly long U.S. dollars.\par     The figures include positions held through non-deliverable\par forwards (NDFs).\par     The survey findings are provided below (positions\par in U.S. dollar versus each \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ):\par \par \par  DATE     CNY   KRW   SGD   IDR   TWD   INR   MYR   PHP   THB\par  18-Aug  -0.04 -1.08 -0.47 -0.81 -0.90 -0.60 -0.33 -0.49 -0.69\par  4-Aug    0.12 -1.01 -0.52 -0.84 -0.67 -0.56  0.16 -0.04 -0.56\par  21-July  1.01 -0.50  0.06 -0.63 -0.37  0.11  0.04  0.10 -0.20\par  7-July   1.12 -0.11 -0.38 -0.69  0.09  0.24  0.06  0.18 -0.10\par  23-Jun   0.51 -0.12 -0.47 -0.44 -0.03  0.32  0.11 -0.02 -0.04\par  9-Jun    0.49  0.14 -0.03 -0.20  0.08 -0.05  0.30 -0.16  0.12\par  26-May   0.96  1.22  0.74  0.75  0.79  0.48  1.08  0.35  0.91\par  12-May   0.52  0.75  0.57 -0.08  0.51 -0.22  0.46  0.28  0.24\par  28-Apr   0.02 -0.36 -0.21 -0.25 -0.06 -0.46 -0.30  0.26 -0.03\par  14-Apr  -0.20 -0.72 -0.57 -0.42 -0.23 -0.38 -0.75 -0.40 -0.16\par  31-Mar  -0.13 -0.96 -0.78 -0.39 -0.39 -0.30 -0.93 -0.69 -0.12\par     \par \par \par ($1 = 31.4150 Taiwan dollars)\par \par  (Reporting by Jongwoo Cheon; Additional reporting by Shaloo\par Shrivastava in BENGALURU; Editing by Shri Navaratnam)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-8-18T08:19:04.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160818ec8i00bte\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
