\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Solid U.S. jobs data weigh on Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; carry interest remains\b0\par\par\uc2 848 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 2016\par 07:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Won firm after S&P upgrade; wary of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     * Yuan down as July \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exports, imports disappoint\par     * Baht down on bond outflows; BOT sees no need to cut rates\par     * Thai stocks hit 16-mth high after referendum\par \par  (Sure(Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 8 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par slid on Monday as strong U.S. jobs data slightly raised\par expectations of a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  interest rate hike this year,\par while sustained appetite for higher yields in the region limited\par their losses.\par     The South Korean won, however, turned higher\par after a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  sovereign rating upgrade. \par     China's yuan fell as trade data showed both\par imports and exports for the world's second largest economy fell \par faster than economists had expected.  \par     The Thai baht recovered some losses after hitting a\par near two-week low as local stocks touched a 16-month peak with\par Thais voting in a referendum to accept a new military-backed\par constitution. Earlier, the baht came under pressure\par from bond outflows.\par     Malaysian's ringgit slid on low government bond\par prices.\par     U.S. employers added 255,000 jobs in July, higher than a\par forecast of 180,000 increase, after an upwardly revised 292,000\par surge in June, data showed on Friday. \par     The data slightly increased odds of U.S. rate hikes, but the\par Fed may stay cautious over tightening, given uncertainties\par arising from Brexit and a slowing China's economy, analysts\par said. \par     Fed funds rate futures are pricing in less than a 20 percent\par chance that the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will raise rates in its next\par policy meeting in September and less than a 50 percent chance\par even by the end of year.\par     "The payrolls were much stronger than expected and talks of\par U.S. rate hike expectations were back on the table," said\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Christopher Wong\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for Maybank in\par Singapore.\par     "The talks remain preliminary at this stage. Given the\par environment of accommodative monetary conditions and potential\par Fed delay, EM carry trades could still be the theme to play,"\par said Wong, adding the Indonesia's rupiah and the Indian rupee\par are seen major beneficiaries for a medium term.\par     \par     WON\par     The won started the day weaker as South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were on Friday suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weaker than 1,110 per dollar, traders said.\par     But it turned stronger after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  upgraded the\par South Korea's sovereign rating to AA from AA- with stable\par outlook.\par     Exporters were already buying the won for settlements, while\par offshore funds bought the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on dips.\par     \par     BAHT\par     The baht earlier lost nearly 0.6 percent to 35.012 per\par dollar, its weakest since July 27, with most government bonds\par  down.\par     Thailand's central governor told Reuters in an interview\par that there is no immediate need to cut interest rates to\par stimulate growth as liquidity remains ample. \par     Foreign investors were net sellers of the local bonds in the\par previous three consecutive sessions, especially long-term notes,\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thai Bond Market Association\f28 \uc2 \f2  data showed.\par     Some of them may not want to add more Thai debt holdings as\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's stance could reduce chances of capital gains\par from bonds.\par     The Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pared some of earlier losses as Bangkok\par shares jumped more than 1 percent with the referendum\par seen reducing political uncertainty in the country.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit slid as most of Malaysia's government bond\par prices slumped.\par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recovered some of earlier losses,\par tracking rises in oil prices, while sentiment towards on the\par ringgit remained weak.\par     A senior Malaysian bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader said he was looking\par to sell the ringgit around 4.0300 per dollar for a target of\par 4.0700. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stood at 4.0400 in the early afternoon.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0505 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest bid   Previous day  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                   101.99         101.82     -0.17\par   Sing dlr                    1.3468         1.3461     -0.05\par   Taiwan dlr                  31.539         31.570     +0.10\par   Korean won                 1110.20        1110.40     +0.02\par   Baht                        