\par\par \b \uc2 POLL- \highlight22\uc2 China interventions \highlight\uc2  grinding down yuan bears, inflows boost Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  bulls\b0\par\par\uc2 820 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 2016\par 08:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Yuan short positions smallest since late April on \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par     * Won, rupiah views most optimistic in over 2 yrs on inflows\par     * Baht, Taiwan dollar bullish bets largest since 2013\par \par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 4 (Reuters) - Bearish bets on the Chinese\par yuan fell to a more than three-month low in the last two weeks\par as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stabilised the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after it fell\par through a key psychological level, a Reuters poll showed.\par     Sentiment on most other emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  grew even\par more positive, meanwhile, as global investors continued to flock\par to the region's stock and bond markets in search of higher\par yields.\par     Bullish bets on some regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were the highest in\par two to three years, according to the poll of 20 fund managers,\par analysts and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders conducted from Tuesday through\par Thursday. (GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2aDRP78"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2aDRP78}}}\uc2 \f2 )\par     Bets on further declines in the yuan shrank to\par the smallest since late April, when sentiment on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par was nearly neutral, according to the survey.\par     Last month, the renminbi weakened past the psychologically\par important 6.7 per dollar mark, nearing six-year lows. But it has\par rebounded 1 percent since then as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par slow down the pace of its depreciation. Recent dollar weakness\par has also helped the yuan rebound.\par     Still, the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may fall more than 3 percent\par against the dollar over the next 12 months, given the slowdown\par in the world's second-largest economy, a separate Reuters poll\par showed on Wednesday. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  will allow it to\par resume weakening, analysts said. \par     Disappointing U.S. data in the last few weeks, especially\par second-quarter economic growth, has caused investors to scale\par back expectations of a near-term interest rate hike by the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 , taking steam out of the dollar.\par     Other major monetary authorities including the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  are expected to ease policy\par further in the wake of Britain's vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European\par Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     Such stimulus is expected to push more capital into emerging\par Asia as investors scour the world for better yields.\par     The Indonesia rupiah - which offers one of highest\par yields in Asia - saw the largest bullish bets since April 2014.\par     South Korea's won saw the highest long positions\par since July 2014 on equity inflows.\par     Optimistic bets on the Thai baht increased to the\par largest since April 2013 on capital inflows, while the Taiwan\par dollar saw the highest bullish bets since January 2013.\par     Foreign demand for Indian stocks and bonds lifted the\par rupee's long positions to the largest since April 2015.\par     The Malaysian ringgit bucked the trend, however,\par with short positions edging up on concerns over scandal-plagued\par state fund \f28 \uc2 \f2 1Malaysia Development Berhad\f28 \uc2 \f2  and weak oil prices.\par     The poll is focused on what analysts and fund managers\par believe are the current market positions in nine Asian emerging\par market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : the Chinese yuan, South Korean won, Singapore\par dollar, Indonesian rupiah, Taiwan dollar, Indian rupee,\par Philippine peso, Malaysian ringgit and the Thai baht.\par     The poll uses estimates of net long or short positions on a\par scale of minus 3 to plus 3. A score of plus 3 indicates the\par market is significantly long U.S. dollars.\par     The figures include positions held through non-deliverable\par forwards (NDFs).\par     The survey findings are provided below (positions\par in U.S. dollar versus each \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ):\par \par \par  DATE     CNY   KRW   SGD   IDR   TWD   INR   MYR   PHP   THB\par  4-Aug    0.12 -1.01 -0.52 -0.84 -0.67 -0.56  0.16 -0.04 -0.56\par  21-July  1.01 -0.50  0.06 -0.63 -0.37  0.11  0.04  0.10 -0.20\par  7-July   1.12 -0.11 -0.38 -0.69  0.09  0.24  0.06  0.18 -0.10\par  23-Jun   0.51 -0.12 -0.47 -0.44 -0.03  0.32  0.11 -0.02 -0.04\par  9-Jun    0.49  0.14 -0.03 -0.20  0.08 -0.05  0.30 -0.16  0.12\par  26-May   0.96  1.22  0.74  0.75  0.79  0.48  1.08  0.35  0.91\par  12-May   0.52  0.75  0.57 -0.08  0.51 -0.22  0.46  0.28  0.24\par  28-Apr   0.02 -0.36 -0.21 -0.25 -0.06 -0.46 -0.30  0.26 -0.03\par  14-Apr  -0.20 -0.72 -0.57 -0.42 -0.23 -0.38 -0.75 -0.40 -0.16\par  31-Mar  -0.13 -0.96 -0.78 -0.39 -0.39 -0.30 -0.93 -0.69 -0.12\par  17-Mar   0.21 -0.08 -0.01 -0.59  0.06  0.08 -0.26 -0.47 -0.16\par     \par \par  (Additional reporting by Shaloo Shrivastava in BENGALURU;\par Editing by Kim Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-8-4T07:44:22.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA000002016080