\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan firms against dollar but weakens against  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  basket\b0\par\par\uc2 588 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2016\par 06:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, July 26 (Reuters) - China's yuan firmed against\par the dollar on Tuesday following a firmer guidance rate setting\par from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and a weaker dollar index, but it\par weakened against a calculated basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  following\par five days of gains.\par     The yuan's sharp firming against a trade-weighted basket of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  began last week amid a meeting of finance heads from\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Group of 20\f28 \uc2 \f2  economies in Chengdu.\par     China won plaudits during the meeting for improving the\par transparency of its fixing mechanism that brought its daily\par midpoint setting more in line with market trading. However,\par traders believe the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 still\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to keep the onshore spot from crossing\par the psychologically important 6.7 per dollar.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate at 6.6778 per\par dollar prior to market open, firmer than the previous fix 6.686.\par Traders have recently pointed out the midpoint was being used to\par drag the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher, although Tuesday's setting has aligned\par with trader forecasts.\par     "The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has stepped up \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep the yuan\par stable, in particular managing the closing rates," said a dealer\par at a European bank in Shanghai. \par     "With the closing rates officially managed, the midpoint is\par also under the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  control. In addition to a relatively\par stable dollar index, the yuan has been able to maintain\par stability of late."\par     The spot market opened at 6.6780 per dollar and\par was changing hands at 6.6793 at midday, 13 pips away from the\par previous late session close and 0.02 percent away from the\par midpoint. The spot rate is currently allowed to trade within a 2\par percent range above or below the official fixing on any given\par day.\par     The Thomson Reuters/HKEX Global CNH index, which\par tracks the offshore yuan against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on a\par daily basis, stood at 95.97, weaker than the previous day's\par 96.1. \par     The global dollar index fell to 97.17 from the\par previous close of 97.286. \par     The offshore yuan was trading -0.11 percent away from the\par onshore spot at 6.6867 per dollar. \par     Offshore one-year non-deliverable forwards contracts\par (NDFs), considered the best available proxy for\par forward-looking market expectations of the yuan's value, traded\par at 6.841, -2.39 percent away from the midpoint.\par     One-year NDFs are settled against the midpoint, not the spot\par rate.\par \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE SPOT:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  PBOC midpoint      6.6778   6.686     0.12%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.6793   6.6806    0.02%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.02%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change YTD                       -2.78%\par  Spot change since 2005                23.91%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par     Key indexes:\par      \par  Item            Current     Previous  Change\par                                        \par  Thomson         95.97       96.1      -0.1\par  Reuters/HKEX                          \par  CNH index                             \par  Dollar index    97.17       97.286    -0.1\par  \par     \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.6867    -0.11%\par         *                        \par  Offshore              6.841     -2.39%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par .\par     \par \par     \par  (Reporting by Pete Sweeney and Lu Jianxin; Editing by Sam\par Holmes)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-7-26T05:30:48.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160726ec7q008ya\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
