\par\par \b \uc2 Brexit front and centre as G20 finance heads meet in China\b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2016\par 04:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CHENGDU, China, July 23 (Reuters) - Finance officials from the world's major economies start a two-day meeting in China on Saturday where they will confront challenges to global growth from Britain's decision to leave the \uc2 European Union\uc2  and consider deeper structural reforms.\par \par \uc2 Worries over \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation will also factor into the discussions, but a U.S. official indicated that the depreciation of China's yuan to five-and-a-half year lows, and the \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reaction, were understandable.\par \par \uc2 The spectre of protectionism, highlighted by U.S. Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's "America First" rhetoric and talk of reworking or quitting trade agreements, will also hang over the finance ministers and central bankers from the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  as they consider ways to spur sustainable growth.\par \par \uc2 The G20 officials' meeting in the southwestern Chinese city of Chengdu will be a debut of sorts for Britain's newly-appointed finance minister Philip Hammond, who will be grilled about the UK's plans for keeping up economic growth.\par \par \uc2 "There will be a lot of attention to this meeting as we gather for the first time since the Brexit vote shook markets," said one Asian finance official.\par \par \uc2 "I expect G20 debate to focus more on potential effects from Brexit on the real economy in the longer term, which should be a matter of concern for emerging economies."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  this week cut its global growth forecasts because of the UK Brexit vote, saying that uncertainty over Britain's future trade relationship with Europe will stall investment and sap consumer confidence.\par \par \uc2 Data out of Britain on Friday seemed to bear out fears. A business activity index posted its biggest drop in its 20-year history, a sign that Britain's economy appears to be shrinking at the fastest rate since the financial crisis in the wake of last month's Brexit vote.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, Hammond said the UK could reset fiscal policy if necessary, his strongest comments to date on how policy may change after Britain's historic decision to leave the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  appear poised to be less of a hot-button issue than they were when the finance heads met in Shanghai in February. At that meeting, China had to counter concerns about the possibility it would devalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and spark a global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war.\par \par \uc2 A senior \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  official signalled on Thursday that U.S. Treasury Secretary Jack Lew was not likely to give China a hard time about the drop in the yuan to five-and-a-half year lows, noting that the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the slide.\par \par \uc2 "Their \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been consistent to a transition to a market-oriented exchange rate and it hasn't had the character of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that we would say by design is to try and gain an unfair advantage," the official said.\par \par \uc2 "It wouldn't be fair to say that over the last few months the downward movement of the RMB was something that was fundamentally driven by policy decisions."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Elias Glenn, Kevin Yao, Gernot Heller, Jan Strupczewski and William Schomberg; Writing by John Ruwitch; Editing by Jacqueline Wong) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-7-23T03:17:21.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160723ec7n002mi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
