\par\par \b \uc2 Chinese Shares Down on Weakening Yuan Concerns -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,894 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2016\par 05:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0327 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] China shares edge down Tuesday, as lackluster economic data in the second quarter weigh on investor confidence, while a weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  further dents risk appetite. The Shanghai Composite Index slips 0.6% to 3025.54, though shares in the aviation sector broadly recovered after global oil prices settled down on Monday as Turkey-related supply worry eases off. \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  fixed the mid-point reference rate of 6.6971 for onshore yuan against U.S. dollar, the lowest yuan level in six years. The earlier share rally was propelled by rising hopes for easing measures around the globe and greater appetite for safe haven assets. Yet analysts caution whether those hopes will actually materialize, in particular after the U.K. decided to keep its rates steady. "We think the door for the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  to reduce rates further has been closed as the focus of the policy this year is centered on supply side reform," according to a research report by \uc2 Guoyuan Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  (Yifan.xie@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0313 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] New Zealand exotic plantation forestry area contracted through 2015 although this may not last much longer as carbon prices in New Zealand have risen dramatically, says the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Department of Agriculture\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a note. It says that carbon prices are now over NZ$17/ton from a low NZ$1/ton the last two years, from a low of NZ$1/ton carbon to NZ$17/ton over the last two years which is likely to stimulate new planting. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 USDA\f28 \uc2 \f2  notes that the log harvest for the year ending September 2015 is at 29.33 million cubic meters of logs just below the previous year but is 50% greater than a decade ago. (lucy.craymer@wsj.com; Twitter: @lucy_craymer) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0306 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/JPY is weaker at 105.90, with investors locking in profits after the pair's recent rapid rise to above the 106-line. But it's premature to determine that the USD/JPY has entered into another downtrend, as long as the pair stays above the five-day moving average of 105.25, says IG Securities market analyst Junichi Ishikawa. The dollar is moving in a range reflecting an adjustment to the recent rally, says Ishikawa, adding that the USD/JPY still has potential to test the upside with support from U.S. stocks, if corporate earnings releases later this week show brisk results. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0252 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily in the market to push the yuan back above a key psychological level that was briefly breached overnight and earlier Tuesday morning, traders say. The dollar is now trading at CNY6.6985, versus CNY6.6987 at Monday afternoon's official close. The pair, however, fell below the key 6.7000 level in after-hours trading. It also opened at an intraday high of 6.7011 Tuesday morning, before quickly coming down on what traders describe as big yuan buying orders from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  through the nation's largest state lenders. "The yuan opened below 6.7000 probably because the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  folks weren't fully ready for work yet," said a Shanghai-based senior trader at a domestic bank. He said the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's apparent approach of ignoring the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's performance in the after hours and focusing solely on controlling its movement before 4:30 PM when the day's official close is calculated is problematic. "We now have a tightly controlled market before 4:30 in the afternoon and a free market after that. It's an unsustainable contradiction," the senior trader added. (hong.shen@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0224 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Gold continues to tread water amid rising chances of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  increasing interest rates, though the possible timing of such a move remains far from certain. The precious metal has paused after rallying strongly since Brexit."However, some of the price increase was driven by speculation, which implies some scope for a correction," says a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  report. "Even so, the gold price is unlikely to drop to pre-Brexit levels," it says, adding the year-end price forecast is $1,350/oz. Gold is currently trading at $1,330.52/oz, 0.13% higher than the previous close. (biman.mukherji@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0222 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Yields of government bonds in the Asia-Pacific region grind lower Tuesday morning as resurgence in foreign demand for emerging markets assets over the past two months continues. 10-year debt yields of Australia fell 6.2 basis points hovering at 1.94% as market is expecting a likely rate cut by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  in August while South Korea's 10-year debt fell 1.8 basis points to 1.397%, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thomson Reuters\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Yields fall as bond prices rise. Citi says Indonesia's bond auction today shall reflect investors' appetite for duration. "Fundamentals--low inflation, high real rates, expected inflows from tax amnesty, expectations of further rate cuts etc.--remain supportive of Indonesian bonds," says Citi, which remains overweight duration in Indonesia in its EM bond portfolio. 10-year debt of Indonesia is down 0.5 basis points hovering at 7.113%. (carol.chan@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0216 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The AUD/JPY is weaker now at 79.50, after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  left the door open to a rate cut next month. The AUD/JPY touches an intraday low of 79.38 from 80.58 late Monday in New York. In the minutes of its July 5 board meeting, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  says it will review this month's inflation, housing and employment data to assess whether a change in policy is needed. "The minutes suggest the RBA may take action," says Takuya Kawabata, analyst at Gaitame.Com Research Institute, adding that he tips the AUD/JPY's downside support at 78.80 and 77.30.(hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0214 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The EUR/USD is running low on technical momentum as it continues to hug its 200-day moving average line at 1.1084. The euro has been flitting around that chart barrier for the past three days, lacking strong trading cues. The heightened volatility seen in the post-Brexit week has disappeared. The next potential driver for the EUR/USD may come from the yen, which exerts its influence via the commonly-traded EUR/JPY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pair. The weakening of the yen may be the most obvious trade idea in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market for now, due to expectations of fresh fiscal stimulus measures from Japan. The EUR/JPY has been edging into a bullish chart formation, which could pull the EUR/USD along with it. If the EUR/USD ends the day above the 1.1109 chart barrier -- the 20-day Bollinger mid-resistance line -- bullish potential will increase. The EUR/USD is now 1.1070 from its Monday closing of 1.1071. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0208 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Bank of Korea Governor Lee Ju-yeol is calling for a cautious approach to the accommodative monetary policy he currently supports for the recovery of growth in the country. "Especially, in the case of small open economies, we need to bear in mind that, if the degree of monetary easing is excessive, the risk that external shocks would trigger sudden capital outflows and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation is relatively higher," Lee says in speech to a forum in Seoul Tuesday. The BOK last week kept its base rate unchanged at a record-low 1.25% even though it trimmed its growth outlook for this year. The BOK decision suggests the bank is taking time out to assess the effects of the latest policy easing, which included a rate cut in June and the government's planned fiscal stimulus on the economy. (kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0204 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 SoftBank Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 's $32 billion bid for UK-based chip-designer ARM seems to have moved \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, as SoftBank converted much yen into British pounds to in preparation for the bid. The upshot: the GBP/JPY spurted up 10%, with a weaker yen causing a 6% jump in USD/JPY. Nomura chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Yunosuke Ikeda says in a note the all-cash deal coincided with "extremely strong demand" for the GBP/JPY buying last week, with speculative money betting on helicopter money in Japan. The fact that the USD/JPY and the GBP/JPY have already got a short-term boost means these pair's upside will likely be limited, says Ikeda. "We need to stay alert to the downside risk on disappointment about the government's economic stimulus," he says. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0158 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/JPY Intraday: Turning up. The pair managed to hold the upside and reached 106.33 this morning. While it is currently off that high, it is seeking support from the 50-period (30-minute chart) moving average. In fact, the 20-period moving average remains above the 50-period one, helping to maintain the bullish bias. If the pair succeeds in breaking above the high seen this morning, it could proceed further to the first upside target at 107.00 (a level above that seen just before the Brexit vote in June). However, a break below the key support at 105.25 would trigger a further decline toward 104.60 (around the low of July 15). [This piece contains the opinions of Trading Central and does not constitute personalized investment advice or form part of any invitation or inducement to buy or sell any security. The author has been prohibited by Trading Central from purchasing or otherwise directly or indirectly acquiring any direct or indirect beneficial ownership of any instruments or markets for which Trading Central or its affiliates issues recommendations. To read more, visit bit.ly/1MehCU9] (analysts@tradingcentral.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 18 Jul 2016 23:27 ET \par Chinese Shares Down on Weakening Yuan Concerns -- -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0157 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] EUR/USD Intraday: The pair continues to trade below the key resistance at 1.1100 and has just fallen below the 20-period moving average. The relative strength index stays below the neutrality level of 50, showing a lack of upward momentum for the pair. In case the pair fails to turn the intraday outlook bullish by breaking above the key resistance at 1.1100, it should return to the first downside target at 1.1025 (around the low of July 15) before slumping further to the key 1.1000 level. [This piece contains the opinions of Trading Central and does not constitute personalized investment advice or form part of any invitation or inducement to buy or sell any security. The author has been prohibited by Trading Central from purchasing or otherwise directly or indirectly acquiring any direct or indirect beneficial ownership of any instruments or markets for which Trading Central or its affiliates issues recommendations. To read more, visit bit.ly/1MehCU9] (analysts@tradingcentral.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July 18, 2016 23:27 ET (03:27 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160719ec7j00056\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
