\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan steady, c.bank strengthens defence ahead of Q2 GDP\b0\par\par\uc2 529 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 2016\par 05:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, July 14 (Reuters) - The yuan was little changed\par against the dollar on Thursday, as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market to smoothen strong dollar\par demand ahead of GDP data this week.\par     The government is due to release economic growth data for\par the second quarter on Friday, which could add pressure on the\par yuan, after June trade figures on Wednesday missed expectations.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate \par at 6.6846 per dollar prior to market open, 0.07 percent firmer\par than the previous fix 6.6891. \par     The spot yuan opened at 6.6890 per dollar and was\par changing hands at 6.6880 at midday, flat from the previous\par close.\par     Traders reported state-owned banks were offering large\par dollar liquidity at 6.6880 per dollar on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to offset heavy dollar demand from clients. \par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has stepped up its defence recently, given\par that client dollar demand has risen," said a trader at a Chinese\par commercial bank in Shanghai.\par     "More and more people are talking about yuan depreciation\par these days and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decided it's time for some\par deterrence."\par     The Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hovered not far from its 5-1/2-year low\par hit on Wednesday last week and has fallen almost 3 percent\par against the dollar so far this year.\par     China's economic growth likely cooled to a fresh seven-year\par low of 6.6 percent in the second quarter as the industrial\par sector loses steam and a boost from financial services fades,\par according to a Reuters poll of 61 economists. \par     "Given that the economic fundamentals haven't changed much,\par I doubt the data would have much of an impact on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market," said a trader at another Chinese commercial bank in\par Shanghai.\par     China's exports fell more than expected in June as global\par demand remained stubbornly weak and as Britain's decision to\par leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  clouds the outlook for one of Beijing's\par biggest markets. \par     Traders said the worse-than-expected trade data had no\par impact on the yuan.\par     The offshore yuan was trading 0.09 percent softer than the\par onshore spot at 6.6938 per dollar. \par \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  PBOC midpoint      6.6846   6.6891    0.07%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.688    6.6882    0.00%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.05%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change YTD                       -2.91%\par  Spot change since 2005                23.75%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument           