\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan firms, cbank suspected of  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2  offshore\b0\par\par\uc2 476 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2016\par 06:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, July 13 (Reuters) - The yuan edged up against the\par dollar on Wednesday, and traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was seen\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the offshore market to ease depreciation pressure\par on the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Traders said the market was little fazed by fears of a spike\par in regional political tensions after an international\par arbitration court ruled on Tuesday that China has no historic\par title over the waters of the South China Sea.  \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate \par at 6.6891 per dollar prior to the market open, 0.09 percent\par firmer than the previous fix of 6.695. \par     Spot yuan opened at 6.6883 per dollar and was\par changing hands at 6.6846 at midday, firming 0.12 percent from\par the previous close.\par     Traders also noted heavy bouts of dollar selling by\par state-owned banks in the offshore market in the morning, which\par resulted in a liquidity tightening in the offshore yuan and a\par brief price spike.\par     State-owned banks sometimes \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on behalf of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  both onshore and off-shore to offset depreciation\par pressure on the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The offshore yuan has fallen through the 6.7 level in recent\par sessions, its weakest since early January.\par     "There's no direct evidence saying the offshore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par is linked to the South \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Sea ruling," said another trader at\par a Chinese commercial bank in Shanghai.\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has already tightened up its defense since\par last Friday, given more and more people are talking about yuan\par depreciation these days."\par     "It looks to us that \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  intends to limit\par the upside of USD-CNY and USD-CNH for the time being, as a fast\par depreciation in CNY could trigger massive short CNY/CNH\par positions," wrote Zhou Hao, senior emerging markets economist at\par Commerzbank in Singapore.\par     The offshore yuan was trading 0.06 percent softer than the\par onshore spot at 6.6889 per dollar.     \par \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  PBOC midpoint      6.6891   6.695     0.09%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.6846   6.6929    0.12%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    -0.07%             \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change YTD                       -2.86%\par  Spot change since 2005                23.81%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Off