\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan slips, c.bank seen controlling pace of depreciation\b0\par\par\uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2016\par 06:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, July 11 (Reuters) - The yuan inched lower against\par the dollar on Monday, but further weakness was capped as the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to offset massive\par dollar demand from banks' clients, traders said.\par     "The rates in the morning were really flat," said a trader\par at a Chinese commercial bank in Shanghai. "State banks were\par offering dollars from 6.6870 to 6.6872. Only 2 pips apart."\par     "I suspect that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is not even willing to let\par the yuan slide to 6.69 at least for now, not to mention 6.7."\par     State banks typically \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market on\par behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , offering dollar liquidity to shore\par up the yuan when the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  faces downward pressure.\par     Spot yuan opened at 6.6889 per dollar and was\par changing hands at 6.6870 at midday, easing 0.06 percent from the\par previous close. The rates barely moved since 9:45 am (0130 GMT).\par     The yuan has now lost close to 3 percent against the dollar\par so far this year and is hovering around 5-1/2 year lows, while\par it has lost more than 6 percent against a trade-weighted basket.\par  \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate \par at 6.6843 per dollar prior to the market open, only 0.01 percent\par firmer than the previous fix 6.6853. \par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has guided the official guidance rate within a\par tight range of less than 0.1 percent change in the past three\par sessions after Beijing pledged to allow greater two-way\par volatility in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year.\par     Traders also noticed that the direction of the fixing was\par not in line with market expectations. The market expected the\par midpoint to weaken slightly but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthened it\par instead on Monday.\par     "This is really confusing," said a trader at another Chinese\par commercial bank in Shanghai. \par     Traders said the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  might let the yuan slide further if\par faced with a surging dollar.\par     The latest China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Trade System (CFETS) data\par showed that the index for the yuan's value based on the market's\par trade-weighted basket stood at 94.25 last week, the\par lowest on record and down 6.6 percent for the year.\par     The index was first published by CFETS in December 2015,\par setting the yuan's value at 100 at the end of 2014.\par     The offshore yuan was trading 0.18 percent softer than the\par onshore spot at 6.6993 per dollar.\par     China will release June trade data on Wednesday and June\par activity indicators on Friday, along with second-quarter GDP. \par \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  PBOC midpoint      6.6843   6.6853    0.01%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.687    6.683     -0.06%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.04%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change YTD                       -2.89%\par  Spot change since 2005                23.77%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.6993    -0.18%\par         *                        \par  Offshore              6.844     -2.33%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par \par \par     \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Kim Coghill)\f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-7-11T05:01:12.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160711ec7b0089h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
