\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Yield-hunting lifts Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , but yuan hits new 5-1/2-yr low\b0\par\par\uc2 677 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2016\par 06:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Yuan falls on lack of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  c.bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     * Baht at 2-mth high on capital inflows; 35.00/dlr resisted\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, July 4 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par rose on Monday in subdued trading as investors continued to seek\par the region's higher yields on expectations that central banks in\par developed countries may ease monetary policies further.\par     China's yuan kept failing to ride on the trend\par and touched its weakest since December 2010 as a lack of signs\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the renminbi indicated the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would tolerate a further weakening of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     Trading in Asia was relatively inactive ahead of the U.S.\par Independence Day holiday and regional festivals to celebrate the\par end of the Muslim fasting month. Indonesian financial markets\par are already closed and will reopen on July 11. \par     Thailand's baht led regional gains, hitting a\par two-month peak on capital inflows and catch-up demand. The local\par financial markets were shut on Friday when most of its regional\par peers rose.\par     "In the lead-up to Brexit, global investors were positioned\par extremely defensively in Asia EM and now these underweight\par positions are moving to overweight," said Stephen Innes, a\par senior trader for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  broker Oanda Asia Pacific in Singapore.\par     "Potentially, massive easing programs from the BOE, \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  and\par BOJ are in the offing, which could prove supportive for regional\par asset markets, amidst extremely buoyant investor sentiment,"\par Innes said, referring to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     Given uncertainty over the long-term impact on the world\par economy of Britain's vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 , global\par central banks are expected to take further monetary stimulus\par moves, investors and analysts have said.\par     \par     BAHT\par     The baht rose 0.4 percent to 35.00 per dollar, its strongest\par since May 3.\par     Thailand's government bond prices rose. Foreign\par investors bought a combined net 113.4 billion baht ($3.2\par billion) worth of local bonds in June, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thai Bond Market\par Association\f28 \uc2 \f2  data showed.\par     Bangkok shares recently found support as foreigners\par were net buyers of 18.4 billion baht in equities last month.\par .\par     The Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has a chart resistance at the session\par high, the 76.4 percent Fibonacci retracement level of its\par depreciation from March to May, analysts said.\par     \par     WON\par     South Korea's won eased on growing caution over\par possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities to\par stem its strength.\par     The won on Friday touched a near two-month peak on stock\par inflows and demand from exporters for settlements.\par     Still, traders were looking for chances to buy the won on\par dips as foreign investors continued to buy Seoul shares.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0450 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid   Previous day  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                  102.71         102.55     -0.16\par   Sing dlr                   1.3442         1.3450     +0.06\par   Taiwan dlr                 32.184         32.218     +0.11\par   Korean won                1145.60        1145.00     -0.05\par   Baht                        35.03          35.13     +0.29\par   Peso                       46.830         46.915     +0.18\par  *Rupiah                      13135          13135      0.00\par   Rupee                       67.20          67.32     +0.17\par   Ringgit                    3.9930         3.9985     +0.14\par   Yuan                       6.6610         6.6575     -0.05\par                                                             \par   Change so far in 2016                                     \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  End prev year  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                  102.71         120.30    +17.13\par   Sing dlr                   1.3442         1.4177     +5.47\par   Taiwan dlr                 32.184         33.066     +2.74\par   Korean won                1145.60        1172.50     +2.35\par   Baht                        35.03          36.00     +2.77\par   Peso                        46.83          47.06     +0.49\par   Rupiah                      13100          13785     +5.23\par   Rupee                       67.20          66.15     -1.56\par   Ringgit                    3.9930         4.2935     +7.53\par   Yuan                       6.6610         6.4936     -2.51\par   * Indonesian financial markets 