\par\par \b \uc2 UK Vote Impact on India: More Noise Than Substance -- Brexit Market Talk -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,911 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2016\par 06:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0441 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Brexit may rattle India's financial markets a bit, but it won't have any major impact on the South Asian economy, says \uc2 DBS Bank\uc2 . Economist Radhika Rao says India's focus will be on the progress of monsoon rainfall, as well as the government's policy agenda, including how much work it could accomplish in the next Parliament session. That said, short-term market disruptions will have to be managed as the U.K. and the \uc2 EU\uc2  renegotiate trade ties. "The situation is quite fluid at this stage and thereby risks of sporadic volatility in the G3 \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and associated shakeout in the global markets should not be ruled out, especially as focus is on \uc2 EU\uc2 's ability to deal with this fresh crisis," Rao says. (anant.kala@wsj.com; Twitter: @anantvkala) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0439 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Citi's private banking CIO says a Brexit will have less economic impact on the world than the 2011-2012 euro sovereign debt crisis did and that the chance of a liquidity shock today similar to the one that started the global financial crisis isn't likely. "These regional problems should stay that way," says Steven Wieting at a presentation for the press in Hong Kong. He compared now to the UK's exit from the European exchange rate mechanism in 1992, which sent the pound lower by 12% in three months and global equities tumbling. The pound was still down by about that amount a year later, but other assets recovered. The reason why markets, including banks, are still selling off this week is simply because of the uncertainty around the UK's future arrangement with the \uc2 EU\uc2 . "Pricing uncertainty often means you price the most extreme form of it," he said. \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 's stock is down 27% in the last six months. (chao.deng@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0409 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sells 2.090 trillion yen ($20 billion) of 0.1% 2-year bonds at the lowest offered price of 100.795, yielding a record low minus 0.295%, in line with street forecasts. The bid-to-offer ratio worsened from the last auction, to 4.95 from 5.52. But the tail, or the difference between the average price and the lowest accepted price, improved to 0.008 versus 0.003 at the last tender. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0407 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Given global upheavals, markets could be forgiven for forgetting the Federal election in Australia on Saturday. The key thing to remember about the election is that all seats in both the lower and upper houses are being contested. It opens the door further for some surprises. Nomura has had a stab at what might transpire. Local polls have remained quite tight and markets still appear relatively complacent, it says. Nomura's base case remains that the ruling Liberal/National Coalition will win the elections, but with a significantly reduced majority. However, recent global trends have highlighted that the polls do not always get it right, it adds. "In a low-growth, low-inflation world, populist revolts against established political parties seem to be becoming something of a norm, raising the risk of days of protracted negotiations with minor parties and independents, in order to form a minority government," it adds. (james.glynn@wsj.com; Twitter: @JamesGlynnWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0357 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China stocks trade slightly down Tuesday morning amid continued yuan depreciation, even as appetite on the small-cap dominated Shenzhen board heats up on renewed chatter about launch for Shenzhen-Hong Kong Stock Connect. The benchmark Shanghai Composite Index falls 0.1% to 2879.14, after losing as much as 0.6%. \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday again set the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixing against the U.S. dollar to the weakest level in five-and-a-half years. The onshore yuan trades 0.1% lower against the dollar to 6.6487. The stocks of some aviation firms suffered due to their exposure to dollar debt, including Spring Airline (601021.SH) and China Southern Airline (600029.SH), which fell 3.4% and 2.7%, respectively. Investors are betting that the regulator will increase the quota for domestic investors to buy Hong Kong stocks. As of Monday, nearly 75% of the aggregate southbound Shanghai-Hong Kong Stock Connect quota has been used up, according to data from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shanghai Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Some speculate that the Shenzhen-Hong Kong stock scheme will be launched partly to ease this quota pressure. Speculative sentiment is on the rise, as trading volumes on the more volatile ChiNext board gained for a third straight session Monday. The Shenzhen Composite Index gains 0.5% to 1957.11 and the ChiNext Price Index reverses 0.8% intraday losses, edging up 0.4% to 2200.46 by midday Tuesday. (Yifan.xie@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0339 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Speculation has grown for policy actions by Japanese authorities to support the domestic economy following the U.K.'s surprising vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 , but there may be limited tools available, says Katsunori Kitakura, strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sumitomo Mitsui Trust Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 . He says yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is unlikely because the dollar has also risen along with the yen. Treasury Secretary \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jacob Lew\f28 \uc2 \f2  says unilateral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would be destabilizing. Options appear limited for monetary easing with negative interest rates being unpopular, Kitakura says. Hopes for bigger fiscal stimulus may be reasonable, he says. Yet, he says, "This isn't a financial crisis, but rather a political crisis," adding it's unclear how the U.K. will proceed with the exit. "Uncertainty has risen, but questions remain whether it would be the best to act now." The Nikkei is down 0.3%. The USD/JPY is at 102.14. (kosaku.narioka@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0330 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Bond traders say the lowest accepted price for two-year Japan government bonds in the 0345 GMT auction result will likely come in at around 100.79. The latest issue (amounting to 2.3 trillion yen), carries a coupon of 0.1%, the same as the previous issue. Analysts said today's two-year JGB auction should be uneventful, due to demand from non-Japanese investors, who recently jumped in Japanese-bond trades thanks to rising returns on the cheaply funded yen. Two-year Japan government bonds last traded at 100.794 Tuesday. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0315 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] After two years of steadily worsening economic conditions in Singapore, recent data paint a possibly more upbeat economic picture for the island nation, Centennial Asia Advisors says. Centennial Asia Advisors is an independent research firm that advises family offices and funds. "In particular, activities related to external demand are picking up and could provide a much-needed boost to Singapore's flagging growth rate if sustained," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Manu Bhaskaran\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chief executive of Centennial Asia Advisors says in a note shared by research house Smartkarma. The comments come after Singapore reported three consecutive months of higher industrial output. Bhaskaran cites the fall in unemployment rate between December and March and surge in tourist arrivals as two other major positives. But he adds that the downside risks, which include tepid domestic demand and disinflation, remain significant. "Singapore needs to uncover new growth engines in order to create new industries for enduring growth and relevance," he adds. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; Twitter: @journosaurabh) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0307 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The yuan's fixing Tuesday is weaker than most traders' estimates, suggesting that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  is using the dollar's strong performance, rather than the opaque basket of multiple \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , to dictate the yuan's direction, traders said. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the fixing at 6.6528 earlier in the day. "This is higher than my own calculation based on the presumed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  basket, which put the figure at 6.6450 or so," said a Shanghai-based senior trader at a domestic bank. "The feeling is that the fixings in recent days have been more of a reflection of the dollar's rally, instead of other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," he said. The latest approach by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  might be a signal that Beijing is happy to allow the yuan to enjoy some passive, dollar-driven depreciation that would help it's slowing economy. "The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  is telling people that, look, we are following the dollar more closely now, so the outlook for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is quite clear," said the Shanghai-based senior trader. By doing this, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has in fact removed uncertainties and anxiety about its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which has slowed panic-driven dollar buying or capital outflows from China, he said. (hong.shen@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0305 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Japan's finance minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taro Aso\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Tuesday expresses concern over the yen's recent surge, but he also concedes that the global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market has maintained overall stability. "Speaking of exchange rates, I think it is correct to say that they have been stable compared with the worst case scenario that we thought could happen" as a result of a Brexit vote, Aso says at a regular news conference. He makes the remark in response to questions about U.S. Treasury chief \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jacob Lew\f28 \uc2 \f2 's assessment reported overnight that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market has been orderly. The development underscores Tokyo's continued struggle to gain support for action on the yen from Washington, which Japanese officials find crucial for carrying out \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  effectively. (takashi.nakamichi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0251 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Japan's finance minister says Tuesday that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  hasn't called on the rest of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Group of Seven\f28 \uc2 \f2  leading economies to orchestrate joint action to support the pound despite its sharp drops following the U.K. vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "The fact is that the U.K. hasn't asked for joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy the pound to support it," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taro Aso\f28 \uc2 \f2  says at a regular news conference. (takashi.nakamichi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 28 Jun 2016 00:41 ET \par UK Vote Impact on India: More Noise Than -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0250 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/MYR is slipping Tuesday, giving the ringgit a modest gain versus the greenback. The dollar is generally weaker against both major and emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as traders price in the possibility, though still slim at the moment, that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  might have to ease monetary policy by the end of the year, instead of lifting rates as officials have previously communicated. The shock result of the U.K. referendum sent global financial markets into a panic-induced selloff, which has triggered several central banks into action. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  has been given approval to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if needed in the yen, while central banks in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , India and Singapore have been suspected of propping up their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Analysts expect the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  to cut interest rate to a new record low soon. If the Fed decides to backpedal on its normalization of monetary policy, it wouldn't be entirely surprising. USD/MYR is now 4.0880 from its Monday closing of 4.1000, representing a 0.3% strengthening of the ringgit. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 28, 2016 00:41 ET (04:41 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160628ec6s000bg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
