\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan weakens to 5-1/2 low as c.bank tolerates depreciation\b0\par\par\uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2016\par 06:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, June 27 (Reuters) - China's yuan tumbled to 5-1/2\par year low versus the dollar on Monday as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par tolerated the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakening after the Brexit by\par setting a sharply weaker midpoint and refraining from\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in trading, traders said.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 weakened the official\par midpoint the most since August 2015 when China shocked the\par global markets by allowing the yuan to weaken almost 2 percent\par overnight.\par     State-owned banks, who often \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in trading on behalf\par of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to influence the yuan's value, did not\par conduct extraordinary dollar sales to support the yuan, traders\par said.\par     "The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has become more accommodative of the yuan's\par two-way volatility of late," said a dealer at a European bank in\par Shanghai.\par     "The sharp weakening of its midpoint today is in line with\par market expectations, while there is no evidence of unusual\par activity by the state banks today."\par     PBOC Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Zhou Xiaochuan\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Friday that a more\par flexible yuan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is important for China's development and\par reforms and monetary policy will be adjusted "in a dynamic way"\par to meet those goals. \par     Prior to market open, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate\par  at 6.6375 per dollar, 0.9 percent weaker than the\par previous fix 6.5776. \par     Spot yuan opened at 6.6360 per dollar and was\par changing hands at 6.6464 at midday, softening 0.3 percent from\par the previous close.\par     The yuan hovered near 6.65, beyond which some traders said\par that, based on their past experience, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might\par stage a major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to arrest yuan's weakening trend.\par     "It is all getting very exciting - this greater\par fluctuation," said a trader at a Chinese commercial bank in\par Shanghai.\par     "The market is testing the tolerance of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par but also knowing that it won't let things get out of control."\par     Others, however, expect the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  would tolerate the yuan to\par depreciate to 6.7 per dollar in coming months, given a broad\par weakening of non-dollar \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the Britain's vote to\par leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  PBOC midpoint      6.6375   6.5776    -0.90%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.6464   6.626     -0.31%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.13%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change YTD                       -2.30%\par  Spot change since 2005                24.53%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.6652    -0.28%\par         *                        \par  Offshore              6.814     -2.59%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par \par \par     \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom and Lu Jianxin; Editing by\par Simon Cameron-Moore)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-6-27T05:34:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160627ec6r007px\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
