\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan slumps to over 5-yr low on Brexit, c.bank suspected of  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 502 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2016\par 11:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, June 24 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's yuan slumped to more\par than 5-year lows on Friday, prompting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as turmoil swept global\par markets in the wake of Britain's vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European\par Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The yuan hit an intraday low of 6.6285 to the dollar at one\par point, down more than 0.7 percent from Thursday's close of\par 6.5795 and its weakest since January 2011 and \par     It later pared losses on suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and closed\par at 6.6140.\par     Traders said state-owned banks were offering dollar\par liquidity in the market during the day - a tactic the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's\par Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 often employs when \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par     "Our mother has come!" exclaimed a trader at another Chinese\par commercial bank in Shanghai, referring to the nickname for the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     Analysts said Britain's decision is unlikely to affect\par China's immediate economic outlook, but prolonged \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market volatility could add to downward pressure on the yuan and\par revive investors' fears of competitive global devaluations.\par     An economic slowdown or recession in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  following Brexit\par could also weigh on one of China's biggest export markets.\par     "Brexit will be a total disaster in China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market," said\par one trader at a Chinese commercial bank in Shanghai, a comment\par that underscored wild gyrations in global markets that saw the\par sterling plunge and stocks put to the sword on Brexit anxiety.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate \par at 6.5776 per dollar prior to the market open, 0.18 percent\par weaker than the previous fix at 6.5658.\par     For the week, spot yuan ended 0.4 percent down. The spot\par market officially closes at 4:30 pm, with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  announcing\par the close. There's an evening session that lasts until 11:30 pm.\par     The offshore yuan was trading 0.33 percent softer than the\par onshore spot at 6.6375 per dollar around mainland's official\par close.\par \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  PBOC midpoint      6.5776   6.5658    -0.18%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.6154   6.5795    -0.54%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.57%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change YTD                       -1.84%\par  Spot change since 2005                25.11%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.6375    -0.33%\par         *                        \par  Offshore              6.792     -3.16%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     \par \par     \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Shri Navaratnam\par and Kim Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-6-24T10:28:13.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160624ec6o0141v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
