\par\par \b \uc2 European Morning Briefing: Stocks Seen Lower; Fed Mulls Rate Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 4,438 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2016\par 05:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Snapshot: \par ======== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stocks seen lower; EUR/USD 1.1288-91; bonds supported; Brent crude $49.40; gold $1277.50\f28 \par \par \uc2 -Japan Grows Faster Than Expected in 1Q\par \par \uc2 -Fed Officials Flag Potential for June Rate Hike\par \par \uc2 -Yen \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Could Hit U.S.-Japan Relations, Abe Adviser Warns\par \par \uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  Economic Planner Vows To Lift Private Investment\par \par \uc2 -EC to Grant Italy Additional Budget Flexibility for 2016\par \par \uc2 -German Court Bans Bulk of Satirical Poem About Turkish President \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\par \par \uc2 -Construction Begins on Trans Adriatic Gas Pipeline\par \par \uc2 -World Powers Urge Warring Syria Parties to Revive Cease-Fire\par \par \uc2 Watch For: \uc2 EU\uc2  inflation data; U.K. unemployment figures; \uc2 ECB\uc2  governing council meeting; U.S. weekly petroleum status report; Federal Reserve FOMC release minutes; earnings from \uc2 SABMiller\uc2 , FLSmidth, SSE, \uc2 Burberry\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Headline News: \par ============= \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy rebounded sharply in the first three months of the year, complicating decisions by Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shinzo Abe\f28 \uc2 \f2  about how much fiscal stimulus the country needs and whether to hold off on a planned sales-tax increase.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gross domestic product during the first quarter expanded an annualized 1.7% from the previous three months, compared with a revised fourth-quarter contraction of 1.7%, according to government data released Wednesday. Economists surveyed by The Wall Street Journal had offered a median forecast of 0.3%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The result came after months of weak economic data, including contractions in two of the previous three quarters, had fueled expectations Mr. Abe would launch more fiscal stimulus and would again hold off on a sales-tax increase planned for 2017.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Three influential \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could raise short-term interest rates at its meeting next month, pushing back against investors who put low odds on such a move.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 San Francisco Fed President John Williams and Atlanta Fed President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dennis Lockhart\f28 \uc2 \f2  both said Tuesday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's June meeting is "live," meaning officials could consider lifting rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dallas Fed President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Robert Kaplan\f28 \uc2 \f2  later during an event in Texas called for rate increases "in the not-too-distant future" and said he may advocate for a move in June or July.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday it was ready to grant Italy additional budget flexibility for 2016, worth 0.85% of the country's gross domestic product.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The decision, which is expected to be formally announced on Wednesday, was anticipated in a letter sent to Finance Minister Pier Carlo Padoan and published by the Italian treasury on its website.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Commission gave its expected go-ahead to Italy's request for wider fiscal flexibility in light of Rome's efforts on structural reforms, increased costs related to the migrant crisis and security investments. It is scheduled to issue its formal recommendations on Italy's 2016 budget on Wednesday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Shares: \par ====== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IG futures suggest the DAX will open lower by 23 points, the CAC by 9 and the FTSE by 12.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shenzhen and Hong Kong share declines lead losses in Asia Wednesday, after a top Chinese official made no mention of a potential trading link between the two cities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Local media had speculated in recent weeks that Zhang Dejiang, the Chinese Communist Party's third-highest-ranking official, would give a firmer timeline for the launch of the Shenzhen-Hong Kong Connect, which traders hope will generate some excitement for China's languishing share markets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 However, Japan shares bucked the trend. The Nikkei, initially lower, gained after data showed that Japan's economy grew far more than the 0.1% expansion expected by economists.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hang Seng Index was down 1.4% and the Shanghai Composite Index lower by 1.8%, while the Nikkei rose 0.6%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stocks fell Tuesday as investors fretted about the prospect of higher interest rates.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A handful of upbeat economic data releases and comments from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials increased investors' expectations that rates will rise this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Interest rate futures -- a popular tool for hedge funds and money managers to place bets on the Fed's policy -- showed Tuesday that the odds of a rate increase at the Fed's June meeting were 15%, up from 4% a day ago, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 CME Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The odds for a rate increase at the December meeting were 71%, up from 58% a day earlier.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Dow ended down 1%, while the S&P slid 0.9% and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nasdaq\f28 \uc2 \f2  lost 1.3%. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par ===== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EUR/USD was just a tad lower in Asian trading, despite positive data for the dollar released in U.S. hours.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A string of stronger-than-expected U.S. economic data, including consumer price inflation, industrial production, and housing starts, has raised the possibility of a U.S. interest rate-rise in June, boosting the U.S. dollar against higher-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EUR/USD was however still in a state of stasis, caught inside a technical consolidation zone. The EUR/USD pair might take on a bearish technical bias and gain downward momentum if it ends Wednesday below 1.1285 and inside the Bollinger downtrend channel.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But if that support line holds up, EUR/USD might continue to gyrate within a range of 1.1285-1.1365, capped by the Bollinger mid resistance line. The next catalysts for EUR/USD may come from the eurozone CPI data for April due later, as well as the minutes of the last U.S. FOMC meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 0250 GMT EUR/USD was at 1.1288-91 from its Tuesday close of 1.1311 and USD/JPY was at 109.35-36. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Bonds: \par ===== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European bonds could see some support Wednesday with stocks set for minor losses.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The latest round of upbeat housing and inflation releases Tuesday drove investors to shed short-term \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  debt and migrate cash into long-term bonds as they raised some concerns over higher interest rates by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As a result, the yield \f28 \uc2 \f2 premium investors\f28 \uc2 \f2  demanded to hold the benchmark 10-year note relative to the two-year note hit the lowest level since December 2007. Yields on short-term notes are highly sensitive to expected changes in the Fed's policy outlook.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Some investors are getting worried that the Fed may raise rates much sooner than the market is currently anticipating," said Anthony Cronin, a Treasury bond trader at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yield on the benchmark 10-year U.S. note was 1.759%, compared with 1.752% Monday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Fed's minutes for its April policy meeting are due after the close in Europe. Investors will zero in on any clues over the Fed's timing for a rate increase in coming months. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Energy: \par ====== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brent crude crawled closer to $50 a barrel in Asian trade as outages in Africa and Canada and production declines outside of the Middle East region fuelled expectations of a tighter supply market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On the \f28 \uc2 \f2 New York Mercantile Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 , light, sweet crude futures for delivery in June traded at $48.47 a barrel at 0310 GMT, up $0.16 in the Globex electronic session. July Brent crude on London's \f28 \uc2 \f2 ICE\f28 \uc2 \f2  Futures exchange rose $0.12 to $49.40 a barrel. Brent prices was last above $50 in November last year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil prices hiked in U.S. trading, propelled by reports that Canadian forest fires forced more oil-site evacuations, threatening to delay the return of at least one million barrels a day of Canadian oil-sands production to the market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Continuing military attacks on oil infrastructures in Nigeria and instability in Libya have also curtailed the countries' oil \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Meanwhile, output from heavyweight Latin American oil producers is likely to slip 2.4% on-year in 2016 by 250,000 barrels a day due to scant investment, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 BMI Research\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 All these factors underpin the upbeat views by \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Energy Agency\f28 \uc2 \f2  that global oil is entering a phase of rebalancing. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  said the market has already flipped into a deficit.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Adding to the bullishness is the expectation for U.S. crude stocks to contract further. U.S. stockpile data set for release later Wednesday is likely to show a decrease of 2.4 million barrels, according to The Wall Street Journal's survey of analysts and brokers. It would be the second weekly decline in a row after a nearly unrelenting stream of inventory additions had put stockpiles at a record high.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Encouraging demand outlook is also prompting buying behavior.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "India demand has been exceptional year to date and demand in China is being supported by increased infrastructure spending in addition to demand for transport fuels," said Neil Beveridge, senior analyst at Bernstein Research.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Construction work has begun on the Trans Adriatic Pipeline, which is expected to bring natural gas from the Caspian Sea to Europe and ease reliance on Russian gas imports.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The EUR5 billion ($5.67 billion) project is expected to supply around 10 billion cubic meters of Azeri gas a year to European countries, enough to cover the energy needs of some seven million European households.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Trans Adriatic Pipeline, or TAP, would transport natural gas from the vast Shah Deniz II field offshore Azerbaijan via western Turkey to Greece, Albania and then across the Adriatic Sea to Italy. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Metals: \par ====== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold prices dipped in Asia trade as traders book profits.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors were still bullish on gold, with uncertainty on whether Fed will raise rates in June.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 0311 GMT, gold was trading at $1,277.50 per troy ounce, down from the previous close at $1,278.85/oz.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to toby.luckhurst@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 17 May 2016 23:55 ET \par European Morning Briefing: DJ Exclusive Headlines; Other Top Stories\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DJ Exclusive Headlines:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Could Have 'Considerable Aftershocks' on U.S.-Japan Relations Says Abe Adviser\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/yen-intervention-could-hit-u-s-japan-relations-abe-adviser-warns-1463540703?tpl=centralbanking"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/yen-\b  \highlight22intervention\b0 \highlight22 -could-hit-u-s-japan-relations-abe-adviser-warns-1463540703?tpl=centralbanking}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump, Republicans Finalize Joint Fundraising Deal\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/donald-trump-republicans-finalize-joint-fundraising-deal-1463537455"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/donald-trump-republicans-finalize-joint-fundraising-deal-1463537455}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 J.P. Morgan\f28 \uc2 \f2  Reduced Some Employees' Access to Swift System in Recent Weeks\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/j-p-morgan-reduced-some-employees-access-to-swift-system-in-recent-weeks-1463520792"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/j-p-morgan-reduced-some-employees-access-to-swift-system-in-recent-weeks-1463520792}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Philip Falcone\f28 \uc2 \f2 's HC2 Makes $1 Billion Offer for Andersons\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/philip-falcones-hc2-makes-1-billion-offer-for-andersons-1463520433"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/philip-falcones-hc2-makes-1-billion-offer-for-andersons-1463520433}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Highmark Sues U.S. Over Affordable Care Act\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/insurer-highmark-sues-u-s-over-affordable-care-act-1463515485"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/insurer-highmark-sues-u-s-over-affordable-care-act-1463515485}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Other Top Stories:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Economy Rebounds Sharply in First Quarter\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy rebounded sharply in the first three months of the year, complicating decisions by Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shinzo Abe\f28 \uc2 \f2  about how much fiscal stimulus the country needs and whether to hold off on a planned sales-tax increase.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/japans-economy-rebounds-sharply-in-first-quarter-1463530307"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/japans-economy-rebounds-sharply-in-first-quarter-1463530307}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Fed Officials Flag Potential for June Rate Increase\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Three influential \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could raise short-term interest rates at its meeting next month, pushing back against investors who put low odds on such a move.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/fed-officials-flag-potential-for-june-rate-hike-1463522149"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/fed-officials-flag-potential-for-june-rate-hike-1463522149}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 China Economic Planner Vows To Lift Private Investment\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's top economic planner said it will work to lift sustainable, healthy development of private investment, which has seen slower growth this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EC to Grant Italy Additional Budget Flexibility for 2016\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday it was ready to grant Italy additional budget flexibility for 2016, worth 0.85% of the country's gross domestic product.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/ec-to-grant-italy-additional-budget-flexibility-for-2016-1463506733"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/ec-to-grant-italy-additional-budget-flexibility-for-2016-1463506733}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Construction Begins on Trans Adriatic Pipeline\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Construction work has begun on the Trans Adriatic Pipeline, which is expected to bring natural gas from the Caspian Sea to Europe and ease reliance on Russian gas imports.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/construction-begins-on-trans-adriatic-pipeline-1463508079"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/construction-begins-on-trans-adriatic-pipeline-1463508079}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 World Powers Urge Warring Syria Parties to Revive Cease-Fire\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. and Russia on Tuesday remained at odds over the fate of Syrian President Bashar al-Assad, as world and regional powers conducted talks aimed at reviving a tattered cease-fire in the war-torn country.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/world-regional-powers-hold-talks-on-syria-1463480882"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/world-regional-powers-hold-talks-on-syria-1463480882}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Nike\f28 \uc2 \f2  Nears Sponsorship Deal With Chelsea FC\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chelsea FC and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nike Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . are in advanced talks to sign an outfitting rights deal valued at $75 million per year for the English Premier League club, a person familiar with the matter said.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/nike-nears-sponsorship-deal-with-chelsea-fc-1463536211"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/nike-nears-sponsorship-deal-with-chelsea-fc-1463536211}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 17 May 2016 23:55 ET \par European Morning Briefing: Market Prices and G7 Calendar\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DJIA      17529.98 -180.73 -1.02% \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nasdaq\f28 \uc2 \f2      4715.73  -59.73 -1.25% \par S&P 500    2047.21  -19.45 -0.94% \par FTSE 100   6167.77   16.37  0.27% \par Xetra DAX  9890.19  -62.71 -0.63% \par CAC40      4297.57  -14.71 -0.34% \par Closing \par  \par Futures: \par Dow     