\par\par \b \uc2 Yen Strengthening Clearly Starting to Squeeze Japan Profits -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,699 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2016\par 11:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0914 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2  ] There appears to be evidence that the yen's rapid strengthening is hurting Japan's corporate sector. Earnings at major listed Japanese companies fell a combined 1.9% in the year ended March 31, according to \uc2 SMBC Nikko Securities\uc2  . That marks the first annual profit decline since the year ended March 2012 when their earnings were dragged down by the earthquake and tsunami that hit Japan's northern region in March 2011. For the fiscal year ahead, Japanese companies--excluding trading houses that made huge one-time losses--expect their net profits to increase 3.8%. That profit increase is better than a decrease but it's lower than the typical earnings seen during the start of Abenomics, and it's a disappointment to many analysts. "Companies tend to make conservative forecasts at the beginning of the year, but they look especially weak this year because there are not many positive factors expected going forward," says SMBC Nikko's analyst Kayoko Ota.\par \par \uc2 (megumi.fujikawa@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0909 GMT The USD steadies after Friday's gains following strong U.S. retail sales and consumer sentiment. EUR/USD rises 0.1% to $1.1322, USD/JPY is up 0.1% at 108.74, GBP/USD is steady at $1.4364, in quiet trade due to a holiday in some of Europe. ING analysts see the USD supported if U.S. CPI and industrial production data on Tuesday again indicate a strengthening economy, while Wednesday's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  minutes may reiterate a "data dependence policy approach." They see USD bid against EUR, CHF, GBP and JPY, with EM \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also vulnerable. However, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says "there is clearly no sign of USD optimism." This would require the Fed to indicate it could "actually hike rates." (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0907 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] Market chatter has it that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again in the offshore yuan market to defend the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against speculators. But Patrick Wu, head of renminbi trading for ANZ, says there is small chance of that happening, at least not to the extent of earlier this year. That is because funding costs for taking short bets against CNH--the offshore yuan--are still low. If the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  had indeed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aggressively--by buying offshore yuan likely through proxy Chinese banks in Hong Kong--liquidity would have dried up, making it expensive to bet against the CNH. Last Friday, funding costs were slightly more expensive--the only sign of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 --but now costs have gotten cheaper again. Now, it's mostly Chinese companies hedging against yuan depreciation, which could send the offshore yuan weaker, especially if the U.S. dollar rebounds, he says. The offshore yuan was as weak as 6.5588 per U.S. dollar Monday morning but has slightly strengthened to 6.5447.(dominique.fong@wsj.com; @dominiquefong) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0907 GMT Primary market activity in U.S. dollar corporate bonds is set to be a busy this week, thanks to a "bumper" deal by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dell\f28 \uc2 \f2  that could be priced this week, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. The group will be looking to finance its \f28 \uc2 \f2 EMC\f28 \uc2 \f2  acquisition with a $16 billion bond issue. In euros, supply should be a "tad lighter" compared with last week's flurry, but issuance could still end up surpassing the EUR10 billion mark, according to the German bank. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com, @tasosvos) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0901 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] China's stock market rises Monday in late trading on improving fundamentals in some sectors, including agriculture, fisheries and renewable energy. Despite disappointing economic data in April, the benchmark Shanghai Composite Index closes up 0.8% at 2850.86, with more than 900 stocks gaining, led by those in the fishery and non-ferrous metals industries. The better-than-expected sales of electric vehicles in April prompted related stocks to surge. Jiangxi Special Electric Motor (002176.SZ) jumped by the 10% daily maximum and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Zhejiang Founder Motor\f28 \uc2 \f2  (002196.SZ) gained 5.9%. Analysts say that the market is unlikely to plunge further as it has already priced in the impact of Beijing's signal last week that it will tighten liquidity supply. The Shenzhen Composite Index rallies 1.7% at 1815.03 and the ChiNext Price Index jumps 1.6% at 2057.86. However, trading volume stays relatively low at 361.6 billion yuan ($55.3 billion) Monday, the fifth consecutive session when the value of transactions fell below 400 billion yuan. (yifan.xie@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0852 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The recent rise in India's wholesale price inflation is likely to keep the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from cutting its benchmark interest rates any time soon, says research firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Capital Economics\f28 \uc2 \f2  . India's WPI inflation in April was up 0.3% year-on-year, reversing a deflationary trend for more than a year. "We think that it will accelerate further over the coming months," says Shilan Shah, India economist at the research firm. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut its benchmark rate in April by 0.25 percentage point to 6.5%, but is expected to hold at its next policy meeting in June. (shefali.anand@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0849 GMT The current efficient frontier is much lower and flatter compared to the 1990-2009 and 2010-2015, encouraging corporate bond-heavy portfolios, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. Efficient frontier refers to the concept of the highest return for a defined level of volatility, or the lowest volatility for a set return. The best expected return today is 3.5% for 5.1% of volatility, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  . This can be achieved with a portfolio that is 75% U.S. investment grade corporate bonds, 19% U.S. high yield credit, 3% S&P 500 equities and 2% cash. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com, @tasosvos) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0842 GMT \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  recommends buying USD/CAD at 1.2870, with a target of 1.3400 and a stop at 1.2720. USD/CAD trades at 1.2916, down 0.2% on the day. The bank cites "weakening risk appetite, limited oil price rallies and renewed weakness in Canadian data." It says the Alberta wildfires pose a downside risk for 2Q growth, while weak Canadian retail sales data on Friday could fuel expectations of more \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  easing. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  remains short CAD versus JPY. It also recommends buying USD/SGD, with a target of 1.44 and a stop at 1.34, citing a strenthening USD and evidence of slowing growth in China. USD/SGD is at 1.3675. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0841 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] Hong Kong stocks managed to end higher Monday even after the Hang Seng China Enterprises Index suddenly fell for several minutes and rebounded in the afternoon. The HSCEI whipsawed possibly due to two reasons spooking the market, says Andrew Sullivan, managing director of sales trading at Haitong Securities International Securities Group. One is that around 2:14 p.m., a large volume of HSCEI futures sold off quickly; the second is a Reuters report that \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may start investigating non-performing loans at commercial banks. "That was enough to worry people," Sullivan says. "But it didn't really impact benchmark stocks like Tencent... Those just carried on trading." The Hang Seng Index closed up 0.8% at 19884, falling short of breaking the 20000 barrier that would have been a sign of momentum for markets to go higher. This week is light on data, and "the market's likely to drift," he says. (dominique.fong@wsj.com; @dominiquefong) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0829 GMT The German bank regulator's move to address increasing risks from low interest rates by increasing capital requirements is good news for investors, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  . \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bundesanstalt fuer Finanzdienstleistungsaufsicht\f28 \uc2 \f2  , or \f28 \uc2 \f2 BaFin\f28 \uc2 \f2  , will be introducing additional Pillar 2 requirements for 330 institutions next month and expand it to 1,600 entities in 2018. These requirements include a dedicated capital surcharge for interest rate risk, the credit rating agency adds. Entities under \f28 \uc2 \f2 BaFin\f28 \uc2 \f2  's direct supervision are largely savings and cooperating banks. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com, @tasosvos) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0811 GMT If investors want to get an idea of how long the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may hold corporate bonds for, they may as well look at the Fed's example, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  . The \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  will re-invest the principal of maturing bonds, according to the Q&A it published on Friday. The Fed's example of rolling maturing Treasurys and mortgage-backed securities shows that the stock of corporate bonds could remain long after purchases have ended, strategists Ramin Nakisa and Kathleen Middlemiss say. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com, @tasosvos) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0806 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  ] The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development\f28 \uc2 \f2  thinks \f28 \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  still has room to lower its policy rate. "There is a case for further monetary easing, as inflation is still far below the new target," says the \f28 \uc2 \f2 OECD\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a biennial economic report on Korea. The BOK has kept the base rate unchanged at a record-low 1.5% since June 2015. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 OECD\f28 \uc2 \f2  downplays concerns that lower borrowing costs may exacerbate Korea's high level of household debt and spark capital flight. But the \f28 \uc2 \f2 OECD\f28 \uc2 \f2  fell short of clearly advising the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to lower the base rate to help spur anemic growth. Korea's inflation has long been subdued, falling far below the BOK's annual target of 2%. Inflation averaged a record low of 0.7% last year. (kwanwoo.jun@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 May 16, 2016 05:14 ET (09:14 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160516ec5g000vj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
