\par\par \b \uc2 European Midday Briefing: Stocks Struggle for Momentum\b0\par\par\uc2 1,223 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 2016\par 12:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par European Markets: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European stocks struggled for momentum Monday following a weak finish on Wall Street and disappointing figures from the Chinese economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 The Stoxx Europe 600 was down 0.5% in morning trade, with trading volumes expected to be light due to holidays across the region.\par \par \uc2 Risk sentiment was subdued after Wall Street reversed early momentum to close lower Friday as a slump in consumer-focused companies outweighed a strong monthly report on retail sales. Major U.S. indexes have been down for three consecutive weeks.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, China's industrial production, retail sales and investment data released over the weekend all came in below expectations, fueling concerns about the health of the global economy.\par \par \uc2 Industrial output rose 6.0% year-over-year in April, compared with 6.8% growth in March, the National Bureau of Statistics said Saturday, while retail sales grew by a less-than-expected 10.1%.\par \par \uc2 "The releases will heighten concern that economic growth in China is continuing to slow even with more aggressive policy easing in place," said Lee Hardman, analyst at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on its website that monetary policy remained unchanged.\par \par \uc2 In commodities, crude oil prices rose in early Asian trade, but analysts said gains were likely to be limited given a lack of catalysts to pull prices in either direction.\par \par \uc2 On the \uc2 New York Mercantile Exchange\uc2  , light, sweet crude futures for delivery in February last traded at $47.06 a barrel, up $0.85 in the Globex electronic session. Brent crude on London's \uc2 ICE\uc2  Futures exchange gained $1.80 to $48.69 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices fell over the weekend due to profit-taking but ended the week higher. \uc2 Nymex\uc2  oil was on its 10th winning week in the past 13 weeks while Brent rose for five weeks in a row in the past six weeks.\par \par \uc2 "Prices are definitely on an uptrend, but profit-taking will keep prices under $50 for a while unless there are any dramatic events that could help rebalance the market," Gao Jian, energy analyst at SCI International said.\par \par \uc2 Gold rose 0.8% to $1,282 an ounce. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par American Markets Outlook: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stock futures were pointing to a flat open, following a weak finish on Wall Street and disappointing figures from the Chinese economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dow futures rose 0.07% and S&P 500 futures rose 0.1%, while futures for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nasdaq\f28 \uc2 \f2  gained 0.08%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Risk sentiment was subdued after Wall Street reversed early momentum to close lower Friday as a slump in consumer-focused companies outweighed a strong monthly report on retail sales. Major U.S. indexes have been down for three consecutive weeks. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  recommended buying USD/CAD at 1.2870, with a target of 1.3400 and a stop at 1.2720. At 0442am ET, USD/CAD was trading at 1.2916, down 0.2% on the day. The bank cites "weakening risk appetite, limited oil price rallies and renewed weakness in Canadian data." It says the Alberta wildfires pose a downside risk for 2Q growth, while weak Canadian retail sales data on Friday could fuel expectations of more BOC easing. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  remains short CAD versus JPY. It also recommends buying USD/SGD, with a target of 1.44 and a stop at 1.34, citing a strengthening USD and evidence of slowing growth in China.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The USD will likely head lower to Y105 or below in the next several weeks, due to the U.S. slowdown, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  worries and difficulty for Tokyo to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the yen strength, said Deutsche Securities chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Taisuke Tanaka. Over the short term, the dollar may not gain downside momentum, partly due to potentially upbeat U.S. data such as housing starts later this week. But "a narrowing of...U.S. economic growth remains as the biggest focus for the dollar against the yen," he said. Tanaka last week revised his expectations for the dollar to reach Y103 at end June and Y101 at end September, from Y105 and Y107, respectively. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =========================== \par Top Stories: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Konecranes\f28 \uc2 \f2  Scraps Planned Merger With Terex Scraps Planned Merger With\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Finland's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Konecranes\f28 \uc2 \f2  is to buy a key unit of U.S. peer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Terex\f28 \uc2 \f2  for $1.28 billion, ending the companies' planned merger after it was complicated by a rival bid and regulatory hurdles.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philips Lighting Unit IPO Could Raise More Than $950 Million\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philips set the pricing for the initial public offering of its lighting unit, saying the spinoff could raise more than $954 million for the company.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Libyan Oil Blockade Partially Lifted\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Libya's divided oil officials have agreed to allow petroleum to flow again between the country's east and west but have yet to end a crisis that is blocking exports, Libyan officials said Sunday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ============================ \par Analysis: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Calling Time on Europe's Austerity Wars\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If fiscal policy wasn't the primary cause of the eurozone's downturn, it is unlikely to be the solution to today's weak growth, Simon Nixon writes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turkish Military's Influence Rises\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A force that once ousted civilian leaders now shapes President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\f28 \uc2 \f2  's moves in Syria and against Kurdish insurgents at home.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K.'s Leading Brexit Figure Likens \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  's Aims to Hitler's\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Boris Johnson described the European bloc as another attempt to centralize European power.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russia Weighs Tax Increases to Fill Budget Gaps\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While the government is spending its oil reserves to shore up the budget, officials privately say that won't be enough to fill the gap between revenues and expenditures within just a few years. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ============================ \par Still To Come \par Monday, May 16, 2016 \par GMT                    Exp   Prev \par 1230 US  May Empire State \par              Manufacturing Survey \par              Manufacturing   9.56 \par              Employment      1.92 \par              New Orders     11.14 \par              Prices Received 2.88 \par 1400 US  May NAHB Housing Market \par              Index             58 \par 2000 US  Mar Treasury \par              International \par              Capital Data \par N/A  FRA     Whit Monday \par N/A  GER     Whit Monday: \par              Financial markets \par              closed \par N/A  \f28 \uc2 \f2 US      Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2   Sec Lew \par              speaks at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Anti- \par              Defamation League\f28 \uc2 \f2   \par              leadership summit \par N/A  US      Federal Reserve Bank \par              of Minneapolis \par              President Neel \par              Kashkari at symposium \par ============================ \par  \par Global News: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Saudi Arabia, Gulf Neighbors Suffer Ratings Downgrades\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Saudi Arabia and two of its oil-exporting neighbors in the Persian Gulf had their debt ratings cut by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service\f28 \uc2 \f2  , as the slide in crude prices continued to afflict the region's economies. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Other News: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Telecom Italia Net Profit Rises\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Telecom Italia\f28 \uc2 \f2  's net profit surged to EUR433 million in the first quarter compared with \u8364\'20\'AC82 million in the same period last year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Flight-Data Issue Involving Airbus Jetliners Uncovered\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Steps are under way to eliminate the hazard, which was discovered after a takeoff incident last year involving an \f28 \uc2 \f2 easyJet\f28 \uc2 \f2  flight departing from Belfast.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 FIFA Audit Chief Resigns in Protest\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Domenico Scala, FIFA's audit and compliance chief and the man tasked with spearheading many of the embattled soccer organization's reform efforts, has resigned from his post in protest.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ireland Hails Moody's Upgrade as Sign of Confidence\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ireland's new government welcomed a decision by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service\f28 \uc2 \f2  to raise its credit rating for the country, hailing the move as a sign of confidence.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Sarka Halas at sarka.halas@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 May 16, 2016 06:28 ET (10:28 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160516ec5g00115\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
