\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen falls on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  warning, stronger risk appetite\b0\par\par\uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Mai 2016\par 13:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Dollar extends last week's gains against yen\par \par \uc2 * Finance minister says Japan ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed\par \par \uc2 * Aussie falls after weak \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade data\par \par \uc2 By Jemima Kelly\par \par \uc2 LONDON, May 9 (Reuters) - The yen hit a 10-day low against the dollar on Monday after Japan's finance minister said Tokyo was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if needed, and as stronger risk appetite sapped demand for traditional safe havens.\par \par \uc2 The yen had reached an 18-month high against the dollar last week, having gained around 15 percent in the past six months in part because of waning investor expectations for a steady increase in U.S. interest rates.\par \par \uc2 That has prompted a ramping-up of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk from Japan, with Finance Minister \uc2 Taro Aso\uc2 's comments on Monday following remarks last week from Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2 , who said it was watching the yen's movements and would act if necessary.\par \par \uc2 Many investors believe the bar for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still high and that the comments amount to no more than verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It's like \uc2 the ECB\uc2  (\uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ). They say they're ready to take action if needed but we've come from 123, 124 (yen per dollar) and we went to 105, and they haven't done anything," said \uc2 UBS\uc2 's head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy, Constantin Bolz, referring to thelast six months.\par \par \uc2 "If I read those headlines, it wouldn't make me buy dollar/yen."\par \par \uc2 A recent \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  report said "persistent one-sided" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by countries to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could see those with big trade surpluses, such as Japan, classified as manipulators - the latest sign that U.S. officials are not comfortable with more dollar gains.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, the greenback gained almost 1 percent versus the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, hitting 108.14, its strongest in 10 days and well clear of last week's low of 105.55 yen. Bolz said that could be mainly explained by a risk-on mood across markets.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index hit an 11-day high of 94.056, having shown a fairly muted reaction to Friday's U.S. jobs report. That left it well clear of a 16-month trough of 91.919 hit last week.\par \par \uc2 "There is little to suggest that we will see further dollar strength from this point on. We've had a little recovery... but I think this is as far as we can go for the time being," said \uc2 Commerzbank\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Thulan Nguyen.\par \par \uc2 Also helping the dollar's slight rebound was New York Fed President \uc2 William Dudley\uc2 , who said on Friday two U.S. rate hikes this year remained a "reasonable expectation".\par \par \uc2 Speculators increased bets against the dollar in the week up to last Tuesday, taking the most net dollar short bets since Feb. 5, 2013.\par \par \uc2 Disappointing trade figures from China on Sunday led the Australian dollar, often used as a liquid proxy for China plays, down half a percent to a 10-week low of $0.7335 (Additional reporting by Ian Chua in Sydney and Masayuki Kitano in Singapore Editing by Jeremy Gaunt) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-5-9T12:21:18.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160509ec59011il\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
