\par\par \b \uc2 Chinese bond yields march higher as default worries grow\b0\par\par\uc2 890 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 2016\par 07:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Broad sell-off in bonds since early April\par     * Expectations of slower policy easing pushes up treasury\par yields\par     * Short-term corporate spreads up sharply since March\par     * Analysts say uncertainties on SOE debt rising\par \par     By Nathaniel Taplin\par     SHANGHAI, April 22 (Reuters) - Chinese bond yields extended\par their three-week long march higher this week, as rising worries\par about corporate creditworthiness and a less aggressive easing\par stance by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  drained liquidity from the fixed\par income market.\par     Benchmark treasury three- and five-year treasury yields are\par now up over 20 basis points since the beginning of April, as\par strong March inflation and activity data have dampened\par expectations about the pace of monetary easing.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  auction yields have consistently exceeded market\par expectations in recent weeks. \par     Corporate spreads have also risen following several high\par profile defaults, including that of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dongbei Special Steel Group\par Co Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a state-owned steelmaker located in the northeastern\par city of Dalian. \par     The rise has been especially noticeable on the short end of\par the curve. The yield premium of A-rated six-month commercial\par paper over AA-rated paper is up more than 20 basis points since\par the end of March, following Dongbei's March 29 default. \par     Analysts said one reason for the sell-off was mounting\par uncertainty among investors over which state-owned companies had\par strong support from the authorities in the event of financial\par distress.\par     "Allowing widespread defaults without transparent criteria\par for selecting debtors who would be allowed to fail, and without\par a robust, predictable framework for supporting lenders absorbing\par credit losses, would risk provoking a 'credit crunch' with\par significant destabilising effects on the economy and banking\par sector," wrote Andrew Colquhoun, senior director at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch\par Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Hong Kong, along with other Fitch analysts in a note\par on Friday.\par     Adding to signs of tightening credit conditions, Chinese\par firms have cancelled more than $10 billion of new bond issuance\par in April so far. \par     Nonetheless, most analysts believe that in the event of a\par true credit crunch, monetary authorities would step in sharply\par to avoid large-scale contagion.\par     "You had a similar situation in 2014 when it looked like the\par trusts were about to blow up," said Duncan Wrigley, Head of\par Research at the economics and policy consultancy NSBO.\par     "If the risks in the market really threaten to get out of\par control, then at that stage they \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  injected a net 680 billion yuan \par ($104.9 billion) of funds into money markets through open market\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this week, the most since January.\par     The weighted average of the benchmark seven-day repurchase\par agreement in the interbank market, considered the\par best indicator of general liquidity in China, was up 12 basis\par points on the week to 2.44 percent on Friday.\par     The 14-day rate was up by a much sharper 37 basis points on\par the week to 3.05 percent.\par     Although analysts have broadly revised down their\par expectations for further easing by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  following\par strong March data, most still expect several more cuts to bank\par reserve requirement ratios (RRR) this year.\par     Rising yields in the bond market, which raise refinancing\par costs for heavily indebted corporates, could hasten that\par decision.\par     "Despite signs of significantly improving growth momentum in\par March, the structural headwinds from housing oversupply, high\par leverage and overcapacity reduction will remain over the rest of\par this year," wrote Nomura economists in a note following the\par March data release.\par     "We continue to expect three more 50 basis point reserve\par requirement ratio cuts and one 25 bp benchmark interest rate cut\par over the rest of this year."\par     China last cut reserve ratio requirements on Feb. 29,\par releasing an estimated $100 billion into the banking system.\par \par Key money rates at a glance:\par   \par                   Volume-wei  Previous    Change (bps)               Volume\par                   ghted       day (%)                                \par                   average                                            \par                   rate (%)                                           \par  Interbank repo market\par  Overnight        2.0500      2.0296      +2.04                      0.00\par                                                                      \par                                                                      \par  Seven-day        2.4360      2.3192      +11.68                     0.00\par                                                                      \par                                                                      \par  14-day           3.0476      2.9482      +9.94                      0.00\par                                                                      \par                                                                      \par  Shanghai stock exchange repo market\par  Ov