\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Fed minutes lift Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; ringgit strengthens on oil rally\b0\par\par\uc2 582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 April 2016\par 07:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Ringgit near 8-month high; weak NDFs cut gains\par     * Yuan up as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's state banks seen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     * Baht gains on speculators, some foreign bond buying\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, April 7 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose on Thursday as minutes of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's\par latest meeting indicated caution among policymakers over U.S.\par interest rate hikes.\par     The Malaysian ringgit jumped more than 1 percent to\par hover near an eight-month high as oil prices rallied. \par     China's yuan rose after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a\par stronger daily guidance rate and traders suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to hold down volatility. \par     The baht gained as traders cut holdings in the\par dollar, which broadly slid on Wednesday, when Thai financial\par markets were closed for a holiday.\par     Minutes from the Fed's March 15-16 meeting suggested that\par the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appears unlikely to raise interest rates\par before June due to widespread concern about policymakers'\par limited ability to counter the impact of a global economic\par slowdown. \par     The Fed's next policy meeting is April 26-27.\par     Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should strengthen "especially prior to the\par April Fed meeting," said Qi Gao, an emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist for Scotiabank in Hong Kong. "We could have two weeks\par of risk appetite." \par     Gao also said China's macro data "could show signs of a\par stabilizing economy, which may bolster risk-taking sentiment."\par     China will release a series of economic data for March in\par the coming week. A Reuters poll showed that China's exports\par likely returned to growth for the first time in nine months in\par March while the pace of bank lending may have picked up.\par  \par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit advanced as much as 1.3 percent to 3.8700 per\par dollar, close to an eight-month peak of 3.8600 hit on Monday.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pared some of its gains as its non-deliverable\par forwards turned weaker.\par     The prices of some Malaysian government bonds \par slid.\par     \par     BAHT\par     The baht rose as interbank speculators bought it on the\par Fed's cautious stance on interest rate hikes.\par     Some foreign investors bought Thai government bonds, adding\par to support to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0530 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid   Previous day  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                  108.86         109.79     +0.85\par   Sing dlr                   1.3481         1.3471     -0.07\par   Taiwan dlr                 32.413         32.442     +0.09\par   Korean won                1152.10        1156.10     +0.35\par   Baht                        35.16          35.31     +0.43\par   Peso                       46.145         46.200     +0.12\par   Rupiah                      13180          13220     +0.30\par   Rupee                       66.42          66.66     +0.36\par   Ringgit                    3.8890         3.9195     +0.78\par   Yuan                       6.4648         6.4819     +0.26\par                                                             \par   Change so far in 2016                                     \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  End prev year  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                  108.86         120.30    +10.51\par   Sing dlr                   1.3481         1.4177     +5.16\par   Taiwan dlr                 32.413         33.066     +2.01\par   Korean won                1152.10        1172.50     +1.77\par   Baht                        35.16          36.00     +2.39\par   Peso                        46.15          47.06     +1.98\par   Rupiah                      13180          13785     +4.59\par   Rupee                       66.42          66.15     -0.40\par   Ringgit                    3.8890         4.2935    +10.40\par   Yuan                       6.4648         6.4936     +0.45\par  \par     \par \par  (Additional reporting by Satawasin Staporncharnchai in BANGKOK;\par Editing by Richard Borsuk)\f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-4-7T06:35:39.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160420ec470148v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
