\par\par \b \uc2 IMF\uc2  Wants More Data From Beijing On Yuan\b0\par\par\uc2 782 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2016\par 07:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par C1\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    (FROM THE WALL STREET JOURNAL 3/22/16) \par    By Lingling Wei \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BEIJING -- The \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  is pressing China to disclose more information about its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  based on standards the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had pledged to follow, people familiar with the matter said, as Chinese authorities resort to more-discreet ways to support the yuan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 In recent months, the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  has turned to the derivatives market to help prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- a shift from its traditional approach of dipping into its dollar pile to buy yuan.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2  is calling on the \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to release more data on its holdings of derivatives such as forwards, which have become the main financial instrument used by the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the people said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders and investors complain that the strategy is making it even harder to figure out Beijing's intentions for the yuan.\par \par \uc2 "The use of forwards can help tame depreciation expectations" for the yuan, said Zhou Ping, chief investment officer at Binyuan Capital Ltd., an asset manager in Shanghai. "But that also makes it more difficult to gauge the true scale of capital outflows and the drawdown of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves for the purpose of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  pledged in October to adhere to the \uc2 IMF\uc2 's special-data-dissemination standards as part of its effort to win the yuan its long-coveted reserve-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  status, said the people familiar with the matter. Disclosing the data also could shed more light on how much firepower China has to keep defending the yuan.\par \par \uc2 An IMF spokesman declined to comment. Media officials at the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2  didn't respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 The derivatives strategy involves the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  instructing state banks to borrow dollars that they subsequently sell. The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  then enters into forward contracts with the banks, which means it will take those trades onto its own balance sheet at a future date.\par \par \uc2 The tactic has several advantages for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : It allows it to burn through its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves more slowly and drain smaller amounts of yuan from the financial system at a time of economic slowdown. It also leaves less evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In recent months, senior Chinese officials have made efforts to communicate more openly. At both the \uc2 World Economic Forum\uc2  in Davos in January and at a \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  meeting in Shanghai last month, senior officials offered public reassurances about China's economy. On the sidelines of China's just-concluded annual legislative session, senior officials gave one news conference after another, touting the stability of the yuan and the government's ability to manage the economy.\par \par \uc2 But while economists and China's trading partners have welcomed the messaging offensive, it also has left many calling for more-specific actions.\par \par \uc2 "Transparency is more than press conferences," Ben Bernanke, the former U.S. Federal Reserve chairman, wrote in a blog post for the \uc2 Brookings Institution\uc2  earlier this month. For China to fulfill its potential as a global economic leader, Mr. Bernanke wrote, it needs to be clearer about its data as well as its rules and policies.\par \par \uc2 Many analysts and investors have grown increasingly frustrated over Beijing's attempt to censor news coverage and information online.\par \par \uc2 Chi Lo, China economist at BNP Paribas Investment Partners, the asset-management arm of the Paris-based bank, said "transparency is also about being predictable and making data more readily accessible by the public."\par \par \uc2 Chinese journalists privately complain that they are no longer encouraged to do investigative reporting that would expose the country's mounting economic challenges and are instead told to focus on "positive news."\par \par \uc2 The data being sought by the \uc2 IMF\uc2  concern the total holdings of forwards and futures by the \uc2 PBOC\uc2 , said the people. Such data reflect future claims to a country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. Many of the world's central banks, including those of Thailand, Malaysia and India, have frequently disclosed the data to the fund.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2  decided in late November to add the yuan to its elite basket of reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which also includes the dollar, euro, yen and pound. The \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started to report some of its derivatives holdings to the fund in December, but the data so far haven't represented China's total positions.\par \par \uc2 Some market participants estimate that China's current holdings of forwards range between $150 billion and $300 billion, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stepped up the use of such stealth \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yuan in recent months.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 22, 2016 02:39 ET (06:39 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160322ec3m000g9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
