\par\par \b \uc2 Banking Shares Push up Shanghai Market -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,675 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2016\par 07:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0612 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Chinese markets reverse losses in the afternoon thanks to financial heavyweights that are propping up the indexes. The Shanghai Composite Index gains 0.5% at 2879.00, while the ChiNext Price Index trades up 0.6% at 2009.79 after losing as much as 1.8% earlier in the day. Banks, and non-banking financial stocks lead the gainers, up 1.8% and 1% respectively by sector. \uc2 Shanghai Pudong Development Bank\uc2  (600000.SH) and \uc2 China Merchants Bank\uc2  (600036.SH) jumped 5.1% and 3.2%. \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Premier \uc2 Li Keqiang\uc2  said that government \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  succeeded in preventing systemic risks, and called for more comprehensive regulatory oversight. (yifan.xie@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0609 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] India's farm sector growth has failed to meet its 4% growth target, hurt by lower food production due to weak monsoon rainfall. The agriculture sector grew by an average 1.6% every year in the first four years of the current five-year plan that runs between 2012 and 2017 against the targeted 4% annual growth, India's minister of state for agriculture Mohanbhai Kundariya said in Parliament. He attributed the low average growth rate to a "setback in the annual crop production" due to insufficient monsoon rainfall for two successive years, along with moisture stress, unfavorable weather, temperature conditions that hurt the output of summer and winter crops. This has resulted in lower incomes for farmers who complain of spiraling debt amid falling food prices both in local and global commodity markets.(vibhuti.agarwal@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0605 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/JPY goes back to rangebound trade--now at 113.42--after rising to an intraday high of 113.56 on remarks by BOJ Gov. Haruhiko Kuroda that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is ready to launch stimulus if needed. "There is absolutely no need to try too hard before the FOMC," later today, says Yuzo Sakai, manager of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  business promotion at Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  & Ueda Harlow. Sakai says the USD/JPY struggles to go much beyond 114 and is vulnerable to downside pressure on profit taking, while the pair's downside is well supported to help it bounce back to 113. "After all, investors are expecting [the dollar] to remain in a Y112-Y114 range, so that the level at Y113 looks comfortable," he says. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0551 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Heavy Industries\f28 \uc2 \f2  (009540.SE) fall sharply after the shipbuilder said it had been slapped with 120 billion won ($100 million) in fresh corporate taxes. The stock is down 7.4% to 106,500 won, underperforming the broader market's 0.1% rise. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai\f28 \uc2 \f2  had fallen as much as 8.3% to a two-week low earlier Wednesday. A company spokesman said the country's tax authorities recently informed \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the world's biggest shipyard by revenue, of the additional tax imposition after looking into its accounting books of the past few years. He added \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai\f28 \uc2 \f2  will ask the authorities to reconsider the tax imposition, given that the company posted huge operating losses for the past two years. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai\f28 \uc2 \f2  and other South Korean shipbuilders have been suffering from a combination of a prolonged industry downturn, a series of order cancellations and a delay in the construction of offshore facilities. With job cuts and business restructuring, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai\f28 \uc2 \f2  aims to return to a profit this year.(in-soo.nam@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0533 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  has changed its outlook for the Chinese life insurance industry to negative from stable as it expects the overall creditworthiness of insurers to deteriorate in the next 12-18 months. "We expect the profitability and capitalization of life insurers to weaken against the backdrop of weaker macroeconomic conditions and falling interest rates," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The key threat to credit profiles will come from lower interest rates as a result of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's effort to sustain growth. Lower rates mean that the insurers will see a significant drop in investment yields. The declining interest rate environment, coupled with the liberalization of participating products implemented in October, will pressure underwriting income, it adds. (carol.chan@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0529 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Thailand's industrial operators are counting on government measures to help boost their confidence after the Thai Industries Sentiment Index falls for a second straight month in February. Supant Mongkolsuthree, chairman of the Federation of Thai Industries, says that while it would take more time for the slow global recovery to gain traction, the Thai government should speed up its work to stimulate domestic consumption and boost farm product prices to help improve industrial sentiment. "If there can be more investments and the government spending is more efficient...the industrial sentiment index will improve even when exports remain weak," says Supant. (nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @nopbkk) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0527 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The New Zealand share market edged lower on Wednesday, with the benchmark NZX-50 index losing 0.23% to 6562.96. Dairy stocks were unfazed by a 2.9% fall in dairy prices in the latest Global Dairy Trade Auction. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The a2 Milk Company\f28 \uc2 \f2  (ATM.NZ) rose 2.2% to NZ$1.84 and Fonterra Shareholders' Fund (FSF.NZ), the listed arm of dairy group Fonterra Cooperative, rose 0.68% to NZ$5.88. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Air New Zealand\f28 \uc2 \f2  (AIR.NZ) rose 0.73% to NZ$2.77 after reporting a 9% on-year rise in passengers in February. Casino operator SkyCity Entertainment (SKC.NZ) continued its recent good run, gaining 2.75% to NZ$4.86. (kate.geenty@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0519 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Premier \f28 \uc2 \f2 Li Keqiang\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it would be "impossible" for China to fall short in meeting its relatively high economic growth targets even as it pushes ahead with structural reforms, avoids massive layoffs and fosters new engines of growth. The premier's comments at the conclusion of the nation's annual parliament come as some economists question whether China can achieve these seemingly divergent objectives in an increasingly challenging economic environment. "Reform and development aren't contradictory," Li tells reporters at an annual press conference. "We should be able to stimulate market vitality and support economic development via structural reforms." (mark.magnier@wsj.com and @MarkMagnier) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0516 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Chinese Premier \f28 \uc2 \f2 Li Keqiang\f28 \uc2 \f2  signals further easing of social security burdens on employers this year, saying "there is still room for lowering contribution rates" to mandatory social-welfare benefits for workers. Speaking to reporters, Li says China still has "ample social-security funds," which means local governments can be given more autonomy to cut corporate and individual payment rates to the so-called "five insurances, one fund," in accordance with local conditions. His comments dovetail with recent decisions by Beijing to simplify the social-security system in a bid to cut business costs. "The purpose of our efforts is to lessen corporate burdens and to put more money in the pockets of our people," Li says. (chunhan.wong@wsj.com; @ByChunHan) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0513 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Japanese bank stocks are down after the Bank of Japan Governor Haruhiko Kuroda said it is theoretically possible to cut the reserve deposit rate to around minus 0.5%. The comments raised some concerns about bank profitability. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Okasan Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategist Yoshinori Ogawa says it is natural for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials to indicate there is more room for easing. That is particularly true after a fall in stock markets after European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mario Draghi\f28 \uc2 \f2  said there would be no more rate cuts. He says there also appears to be broad selling of stocks that were recently bought back, such as banks, steel makers and shippers. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi UFJ Financial Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  (8306.TO) is down 3.3% at 551.1 yen. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sumitomo Mitsui Financial Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  (8316.TO) is down 2.9% at Y3,607. Steel maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 JFE Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  (5411.TO) is down 5.1% at Y1,535.5. Major shipper Mitsui O.S.K. Lines (9104.TO) is down 2.0% at Y244.(kosaku.narioka@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0511 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Economists polled by Singapore's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  predict the nation's gross domestic product will grow 1.9% in 2016, painting a bleaker picture of the economy than three months ago when they predicted a 2.2% growth. A slump in regional trade and a slowdown in China, the biggest customer for Singapore's exports, are among factors dragging down the local economy. The economists predict Singapore's main non-oil domestic exports to grow 0.2% this year, compared with 1.5% growth predicted in the December survey and a 0.1% contraction in 2015. The consumer price index is predicted to contract 0.2%, compared with an average 0.5% inflation predicted in a similar survey in December. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0508 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Only 1% of companies in Japan's Topix 500 index have a "good structure" for their board, based on an analysis by Jefferies. The reasons? Jefferies finds that less than 5% of companies have a majority of outside directors. Many members lack finance, legal or accounting skills, and have served for many years. According to the analysis, more than 90% of board members are Japanese men and one-third of boards are made up of only Japanese men. Jefferies says that banks, brokerages and insurers in the financial sector have the best board structures, and the worst sectors are utilities, transportation and automotive. Nevertheless, Jefferies isn't all pessimistic: "Most boards in Japan are not deeply entrenched. We thus believe steady, gradual change is not only possible, indeed, it has been happening. Over the past two years, most companies have increased the number of independent directors and many have adopted committee structures." (eleanor.warnock@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 16, 2016 02:12 ET (06:12 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160316ec3g000hi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
