 \par      \f28 \uc2 \f2 Guangzhou R&F Properties Co., Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (the "Company") and its subsidiaries (together, the "Group") are principally \par      engaged in the development and sale of properties, property investment, hotel \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and other property \par      development related services in the People's Republic of China (the "PRC"). \par  \par      The Company is a limited liability company incorporated in the PRC. The address of its registered office is 45-54/F, \par      R&F Center, No.10 Hua Xia Road, Guangzhou 510623, the PRC. \par  \par      The shares of the Company have been listed on The Main Board of Stock Exchange of Hong Kong Limited since \par      14 July 2005. \par  \par      These financial statements are presented in RMB Yuan (RMB), unless otherwise stated. \par  \par      The consolidated financial statements of the Group have been prepared in accordance with all applicable Hong \par      Kong Financial Reporting Standards ("HKFRS"). The consolidated financial statements have been prepared under \par      the historical cost convention, as modified by the revaluation of available-for-sale financial assets and investment \par      properties which are carried at fair value. \par  \par      The preparation of financial statements in conformity with HKFRS requires the use of certain critical accounting \par      estimates. It also requires management to exercise its judgement in the process of applying the Group's accounting \par      policies. \par  \par      (a)   New and amended standards adopted by the Group \par  \par            The following amended standards have been adopted by the Group for the first time for the financial year \par            beginning on 1 January 2015. \par  \par            Standards                        Subject \par  \par            Amendment to HKAS 19             Defined benefit plans \par            Annual improvements 2012         Annual improvements 2010-2012 cycle \par            Annual improvements 2013         Annual improvements 2011-2013 cycle \par  \par  \par            The adoption of amended standards has no material impact on the Group's financial statements except for \par            disclosure. \par  \par      (b)   New Hong Kong Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622) \par  \par            In addition, the requirements of Part 9 "Accounts and Audit" of the new Hong Kong Companies Ordinance \par            (Cap. 622) come into \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during the financial year, as a result, there are changes to presentation and \par            disclosures of certain information in the consolidated financial statements. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                                         - 11 - \par  \par      (c)   New and amended standards not yet adopted \par  \par            A number of new standards, amendments to standards and annual improvements are effective for annual \par            periods beginning after 1 January 2015 and have not been applied in preparing the Group's consolidated \par            financial statements. Management is in the process of making an assessment of their impact and is not yet in \par            a position to state whether any substantial changes to the Group's significant accounting policies and \par            presentation of the financial information will be resulted in. \par  \par                                                                                                             Effective for \par                                                                                                           annual periods \par            Standards                                    Subject                                    beginning on or after \par  \par            HKFRS 14                                     Regulatory deferral accounts                    1 January 2016 \par            Amendment to