f the economic cycle. The Group \par plans to grow its investment portfolio over time, and at an appropriate pace, into a collection of \par rental office buildings, shopping malls and hotels of the highest quality and capital value. These \par qualities can already be seen in its existing key properties, which include the Group's office building, \par R&F Center, in Pearl River New Town in Guangzhou, and its shopping mall, Viva Beijing R&F \par Plaza, both of which also enjoy the benefit of excellent locations. During the year, a new shopping \par mall and four new hotels were added to the portfolio, while a further 451,000 sq.m. of investment \par properties of all categories was at various stages of construction. Situated atop the metro station, \par the new shopping mall R&F Haizhu City enjoys the benefit of excellent location. While the pre- \par opening has partly commenced since October 2015, its full \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to take place in \par 2016. \par  \par Park Hyatt, Guangzhou opened officially in December 2015. It is situated above the 53rd floor of \par the R&F Yingkai Plaza, soaring above the new hub and CBD of the city. This hotel is strategically \par located in Pearl River New Town, adjacent to the Canton Tower, the Guangzhou Opera House and \par the charming Huacheng Square. Park Hyatt, Guangzhou features 208 state-of-the-art guestrooms, \par including 36 suites. \par  \par The newly-operating hotels also included Holiday Inn Guangzhou Airport Zone, Doubletree Resort \par by Hilton, Haikou-Chengmai and Pullman Taiyuan R&F Hotel. All these hotels, which are operated \par by reputable international hotel management companies and are characterized by the highest \par hospitality industry service standards, remained competitive in their respective localities. They add \par diversity to the Group's existing hotel portfolio, mainly made up of city-centre business hotels and \par comprising 5-star