          34,000        21,000        134,000        103,000 \par  \par Total                                           2,192,000      1,778,000     3,727,000      3,035,000 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                                 - 31 - \par  \par FINANCIAL REVIEW \par  \par The Group's profit for the year increased by 3% to RMB6.712 billion from RMB6.506 billion the \par previous year. Revenue and profit from property development increased by 29% and 13% to \par RMB40.744 billion and RMB6.178 billion in 2015 from RMB31.651 billion and RMB5.449 billion \par in 2014. During the year, due to the depreciation of both the exchange rate of RMB to US dollars \par and Malaysian Ringgit to US dollars, the Group had incurred an exchange loss of RMB1.21 billion. \par Rental income increased by 4% and brought profit for the property investment segment to RMB380 \par million not taking into account the fair value gains from investment properties of RMB1.106 billion \par (2014: RMB1.638 billion). The hotel \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recorded a loss of RMB167 million as compared to \par a loss of RMB140 million the prior year. The Group's other business segments (including property \par management, construction services and the soccer team) recorded a loss of RMB509 million as \par compared with a loss of RMB379 million the previous year. \par  \par The Group carries out its core business of property development in 19 cities. The following comments, \par with the exception of #7 (on financing costs) and #9 (on profit for the year), relate only to the results \par from sales of properties: \par  \par 1.   Revenue increased by 29% to RMB40.744 billion from RMB31.651 billion in the previous year. \par      This revenue was based on delivery of 3.514 million sq.m. of sale properties in the year which \par      was approximately 11% more than the 3.162 million sq.m. delivered the previous year. Overall \par      average selling price increased by 16% to RMB11,590 per sq.m. from RMB10,010 per sq.m. \par      resulting in the increase in revenue. The higher overall average selling price for the year was \par      mainly due to the two new projects. They were Guangzhou's R&F Ying Yao Plaza and R&F \par      Dongshan Xintiandi which together accounted for 25% of the overall revenue at average selling \par      price of RMB44,630 per sq.m.. Four out of six significant projects (with revenue not less than \par      RMB1 billion) having comparable selling prices in prior year registered increase in average selling \par      price. These projects which accounted for 18% of total revenue included R&F Shangyue Court \par      and R&F New Town in Beijing, R&F Jinmen Lake in Tianjin, and Jiangwan New Town in \par      Harbin and had average selling price increased between 4% to 57% from the previous year. The \par      two significant projects with selling price decrease was R&F City in Taiyuan and Chongqing \par      which accounted for 7% of total revenue and had a decrease of 4% and 16% in average selling \par      price. New projects accounted for approximately 38% of total revenue. For revenue by city, \par      Guangzhou had become again the highest revenue of RMB12.043 billion (2014: RMB4.955 \par      billion) and followed by Beijing and Tianjin each accounting for 30%, 25% and 9% (2014: 16%, \par      27% and 11%) of total revenue respectively. Revenue in Guangzhou increased 143% as a result \par      of the delivery of two new projects. They were R&F Ying Yao Plaza and R&F Dongshan \par      Xintiandi with revenue of RMB4.710 billion and RMB5.386 billion and selling price at \par      RMB50,860 per sq.m. and RMB40,320 per sq.m. respectively. Revenue of Beijing for the year \par      increased by 18% to RMB10.276 billion (2014: RMB8.688 billion). Revenue of Tianjin increased \par      by 6% to RMB3.797 billion (2014: 3.581 billion). The flagship project, R&F Jinmen Lake, \par      delivered 73,060 sq.m. (2014: 175,100 sq.m.) at an average selling price of RMB27,440 per sq.m. \par      (2014: RMB17,440 per sq.m.) and generated RMB2.005 billion (2014: RMB3.054 billion) in \par      revenue. The new project R&F Shangyue Court in Tianjin, recorded RMB844 million in revenue \par      and accounted for 22% of the city's revenue. Of the cities which had revenue in the year aside \par      from the three cities mentioned above, Taiyuan, Chengdu and Wuxi were the cities that saw \par      modestly strong gain in revenue; in Taiyuan's case it was mainly due to the increased delivery \par      of the project, R&F Prosperous Palace, in Chengdu's case, it was the increased delivery of its \par      project R&F Peach Garden and in Wuxi's case, it was mainly due to the new project, R&F City. \par      Three cities had first delivery of properties in the year, they were Meizhou, Fuzhou, and Baotou, \par      which together accounted for 6% of total revenue. \par  \par                                                  - 32 - \par  \par  \par  \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10 Mar 2016 23:19 ET \par HK Bourse: Results Announcement From Guangzhou R&F Properties Co. Ltd. -17-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par 2.   Overall cost of sales and costs of land and construction per sq.m. increased 22% and 22% \par      respectively to RMB7,670 per sq.m. and RMB6,380 per sq.m. (2014: RMB6,300 per sq.m. and \par      RMB5,220 per sq.m.) with the change in sale mix. The range for land and construction cost per \par      sq.m of individual project ranged from RMB29,100 to RMB2,560. At the high end of the range \par      were commercial projects in Beijing that typically carried higher land and construction costs. In \par      the low end of the range were rigid demand type housing in tier 2 or 3 cities e.g. R&F American \par      Dream Island in Taiyuan. The top project in the year Guangzhou's R&F Dongshan Xintiandi \par      also carried high land and construction cost per sq.m. of RMB17,350 and due to its weight in \par      the total revenue, had significant effect on overall per sq.m. land and construction cost. Each \par      of the four main components of cost of sales, land cost, construction costs, business tax and \par      capitalized interest, remained proportionally stable from year to year. In the year under review, \par      land and construction costs accounted for 83% (2014: 83%), business tax 9% (2014: 9%) and \par      capitalized interest 8% (2014: 8%). Capitalized interest included in the cost of sales increased to \par      RMB2.051 billion from 2014's RMB1.540 billion. As a percentage of revenue from sale of \par      properties, it remained stable at 5.0% (2014: 4.9%). The cost of sales also included RMB2.473 \par      billion (2014: RMB1.863 billion) in business tax. \par  \par 3.   As described above, with the cost of sales per sq.m increased by 22% and a rise in average selling \par      price of revenue of 16%, the overall gross margin fell accordingly by 3% to 34% from 37% the \par      previous year. Analysing based on the gross margin by city, gross margin of the key cities \par      including Guangzhou, Beijing and Tianjian were 51% and 28% and 35% respectively as compared \par      to 50%, 38% and 34% the prior year. The gross margins of the three new cities Meizhou, Fuzhou, \par      and Baotou were 30%, 25% and 27% respectively. \par  \par 4.   Other gains mainly arose from interest income. \par  \par 5.   Selling and administrative expenses as a percentage of revenue decreased to 7.1% from 8.9% in \par      the previous year due to selling and administration expenses for the year of RMB2.899 billion \par      stayed practically at last year's level of RMB2.824 billion. Broken down into its two components, \par      selling expenses decreased by RMB15 million to RMB821 million and administrative expenses \par      increased by RMB89 million to RMB2.078 billion. The effectiveness of the Group's cost \par      controlling effort were reflected in these numbers which were achieved through efficient use of \par      resources without compromising on investment in key competitive factors such as manpower and \par      advertising. \par  \par 6.   The share of result of associated companies was mainly derived from the Group's 20% share in \par      the Guangzhou Asian Games City project. The share of results of joint ventures were mainly \par      33.34% in the Guangzhou Liedecun project, 25% interest in Tianjin Jinnan New Town project \par      and 50% in Hines Shanghai New Jiangwan Development Co. Ltd. These four projects mentioned \par      had a combined revenue in the year of RMB6.961 billion which was approximately RMB1.396 \par      billion more than previous year. \par  \par 7.   Finance costs being interest expenses and exchange losses incurred in the year after deduction \par      of amounts capitalized to development costs, increased by 77% to RMB2.154 billion (2014: \par      RMB1.216 billion) mainly coming from an exchange loss of RMB1.21 billion due to the \par      depreciation of both the exchange rate of RMB to US dollars and Malaysian Ringgit to US \par      dollars. Total interest incurred in the year actually increased from RMB5.801 billion in the prior \par      year to RMB6.019 billion with outstanding loans at the year-end of approximately RMB82.4 \par      billion (2014: RMB67.7 billion) and an average interest rate of 7.8%. Aggregate interest costs \par      included in this year's results amounted to RMB4.256 billion (2014: RMB2.756 billion) counting \par      also capitalized interest released to cost of sales of RMB2.102 billion (2014: RMB1.540 billion). \par  \par  \par                                                  - 33 - \par  \par 8.   Land appreciation tax ("LAT") of RMB2.533 billion (2014: RMB1.283 billion) and enterprise \par      income tax of RMB2.176 billion brought the Group's total income tax expenses for the year to \par      RMB4.710 billion. As a percentage of turnover, LAT increased to 6.2% from 4.1% in 2014. This \par      increase was due to two particular projects -- Guangzhou R&F Ying Yao Plaza and R&F \par      Dongshan Xintiandi with especially high gross margin attracting a combined LAT of RMB1.483 \par      billion or 14.7% of their revenue. The effective enterprise income tax rate stood at 26.1% (2014: \par      26.9%), deviating from the standard rate by 1.1% because of permanent differences limiting the \par      tax deductible amount. \par  \par 9.   Overall, the Group's net profit margin for the year was 15.2%, as compared to 18.7% in the \par      previous year, reflecting the change in gross margin from property development. \par  \par Financial resources, liquidity and liabilities \par  \par At 31 December 2015, the Group's cash amounted to RMB21.28 billion of which RMB20.56 billion \par was in RMB, RMB0.63 billion was in US dollar, RMB28 million was in Malaysian Ringgit, RMB46 \par million was in Hong Kong dollar, RMB16 million was in Australian dollar and RMB0.4 million was \par in Singaporean dollar and with total borrowings at RMB82.44 billion of which RMB69.66 billion \par was in RMB and RMB12.78 billion was in US dollar. Net debt to total equity ratio was at 124%. \par The total borrowings were made up of financing from sources which included 1) bank loans, 2) \par offshore USD senior notes, 3) domestic corporate bonds and 4) trust loans and others each accounted \par for 47%, 15%, 8% and 30% respectively. The Group has secured from various relationship banks \par uncommitted credit facilities of which approximately RMB34.79 billion (2014: RMB20.1 billion) was \par unutilised. Such credit facilities indicate that the banks are prepared to lend to the Group up to the \par limit of the facilities when certain conditions are met such as the production of suitable projects and \par specified documents e.g. construction permits. \par  \par The Group has also available to it perpetual capital instruments which decreased by RMB7.6 billion \par in the year. \par  \par Debt Profile \par  \par In July 2015, the Group issued a RMB6.5 billion domestic corporate bond with 5 year maturity at \par a fixed interest rate of 4.95%. Debts due within 1 year accounted for 40% of total debts. Bank loans \par repaid in the year amounted to RMB13.48 billion while new bank loans of RMB17.86 billion were \par procured. The effective interest rate of the total bank loan portfolio at 31 December 2015 was 6.52% \par (2014: 6.76%). Exchange rate exposure was insignificant as non-RMB borrowings accounted for \par approximately 15.5% of total borrowings. Therefore, the Group has not entered into any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign \par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hedging transactions. As for interest rate, RMB bank loans were at normally stable floating \par interest rates benchmarked to rates published by the People's Bank of China. The fixed rate offshore \par bonds further reduced interest rate exposure and therefore no interest rate hedging arrangements had \par been put in place. Overall, the Group has not used any financial instruments for hedging purposes. \par  \par  \par  \par  \par                                                  - 34 - \par  \par  \par  \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (MORE TO FOLLOW) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 10, 2016 23:19 ET (04:19 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160311ec3b000cj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
