\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-TAKE A LOOK-Five world markets themes in the coming week\b0\par\par\uc2 776 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2016\par 08:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Repeats Friday's story without changes)\par     March 4 (Reuters) - Following are five big themes likely to\par dominate thinking of investors and traders in the coming week\par and the Reuters stories related to them.\par     \par     1/ FINE AND DANDY?\par     One of the worries facing market participants and investors\par in a troubling start to 2016 was whether global growth was\par slowing down, or even whether recession was on the cards. These\par fears have diminished, particularly after recent upbeat U.S.\par data. At first blush, February's payrolls numbers looked\par terrific, with 242,000 jobs created against expectations among\par economists polled by Reuters for 190,000, even though earnings\par growth was below forecast. The jobs data immediately revived\par talk the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  could raise interest rates later this\par year, but the reaction in the dollar was muted. Cloud or silver\par lining?\par     * U.S. payrolls surge, bolster Fed rate hike prospects\par  \par     * U.S. seen growing 2.2 pct after jobs, trade data -\f28 \uc2 \f2 Atlanta\par Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par     * U.S. economic data calendar \par \par     2/ UNDER PRESSURE\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meets on Thursday and a year after\par launching QE, and three months on from cutting interest rates,\par looks set to up its fight against deflation. Latest data shows\par annual inflation in the euro zone fell back into negative\par territory in February for the first time since September. \f28 \uc2 \f2 The\par ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  is expected to cut its deposit rate by 10 basis points to\par -0.4 percent and the size of the bond-buying scheme may be\par expanded by 10 billion euros to 70 billion a month, according to\par a Reuters poll. Easing expectations have knocked Germany's\par 10-year Bund yield to within sight of last April's record low of\par 0.05 percent, while the euro has weakened. Rate cut talk has\par also been fuelled by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's decision to adopt\par negative rates. ECB chief \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mario Draghi\f28 \uc2 \f2  has said growth and\par inflation prospects have weakened and that the March meeting\par will need to take the deteriorating outlook into account. The\par main surprise from the meeting would be if, having underwhelmed\par markets with December's easing measures, Draghi did it again.\par     * POLL-More ECB QE and another deposit rate cut likely on\par March 10 \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Draghi points to increased risks ahead of March\par meeting \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2 's policy has not reached its limit - Coeure\par  \par     * COLUMN - \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  credibility at stake as deflation bites\par  \par     * Sub-zero central banks may just chase inflation\par expectations lower \par \par     3/ "IF YOU FAIL TO PLAN..."\par     Another worry this year has centred on how far China is\par slowing down. China's parliament holds its once-a-year session\par in the coming week and has a lot to do. Delegates will assess an\par updated five-year plan and a plan for economic development.\par China is also planning to lay off 5-6 million state workers in\par the next two or three years. Markets will be keen to see the\par latest economic targets, including for growth, inflation, trade\par and employment. The coming week brings February trade and\par inflation numbers.\par     * China's annual parliament meets under economic cloud\par  \par     * China Feb data likely to show further slump in trade\par  \par     * INTERVIEW-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should avoid \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , capital\par controls -ex-IMF official \par \par     4/ WE HAVE TO TALK ABOUT GREECE\par     Euro zone finance ministers meet on March 7 and there is\par bound to be discussion on what to do about Greece. The\par thrice-bailed-out country is again under review by its\par international lenders, who disagree on how much more the Athens\par government needs to do to make its debt sustainable. German\par Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wolfgang Schaeuble\f28 \uc2 \f2 , while acknowledging Greece\par faces a major crisis dealing with a huge influx of refugees, has\par said this is no excuse for not meeting the terms of its bailout\par deal.\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  fate at stake on muddy Greek border as migrants trapped\par  \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 IMF\f28 \uc2 \f2  sees "good progress" on Greek debt, targets unchanged\par  \par     * Germany faces major refugee crisis, but not excuse for\par bailout delay -Schaeuble \par \par     5/ EARNINGS \par     The European corporate earnings season in winding down. It\par hasn't been a vintage one, with the latest data from Starmine\par showing that 47 percent of companies on the STOXX 600 index have\par beaten forecasts so far, slightly below the usual average of 49\par percent beating estimates in a typical quarter.\par     * European corporate events include: Kone March 7, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dialog\par Semiconductor\f28 \uc2 \f2 , RWE, Merck, Paddy Power, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Betfair\f28 \uc2 \f2  March 8\par     * Prudential, \f28 \uc2 \f2 E.ON\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Casino Guichard, G4S, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Adecco\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche\par Post\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Lagardere March 9, WM Morrison, Carrefour, Aviva, Swatch,\par Hugo Boss, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hanover Re\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Amec Foster Wheeler\f28 \uc2 \f2  March 10\par \par \par  (Compiled by Nigel Stephenson; Editing by Catherine Evans)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-3-10T07:13:23.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160307ec3700hqx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
