\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-Yuan eases as parliament meets,  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserve data awaited\b0\par\par\uc2 657 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2016\par 06:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Corrects spelling error in first paragraph)\par     SHANGHAI, March 7 (Reuters) - China's yuan eased against the\par dollar on Monday, giving up some of its sharp gains in the\par previous session, but traders said they did not expect any major\par moves in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  while the country's annual parliament\par meeting was in session.\par     Top officials sought to reassure investors about China's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy as the parliamentary session opened at the\par weekend, but traders remained cautious ahead of the release of\par February \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserve data which could give clues on whether\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is succeeding in staunching capital outflows.  \par     "Trading was active this morning with robust dollar demand,\par propelled by bargain-hunting after last Friday's yuan rise,"\par said a trader at an European bank. \par     "But overall the market remains confident that there won't\par be any big depreciation when the annual parliament meeting is in\par session." The meeting runs until March 12.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate \par at 6.5113 per dollar prior to market open, the firmest fixing in\par two months, and 0.26 percent stronger than the previous fix\par 6.5284.\par     The strong midpoint fixing by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reflected the\par dollar's global weakness with the dollar index against a\par basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  mainly euro, which dropped nearly 1 percent\par late last week.\par     In the spot market, the yuan opened at 6.5102 per\par dollar and was changing hands at 6.5149 at midday, 0.13 percent\par softer than the previous close.\par     It rose an unusually hefty 0.4 percent on Friday, partly due\par to suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to maintain the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's stability during the parliament session.\par     The latest data issued by the exchange, China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign\par Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Trade System, showed that the index for the yuan's\par value based on the market's trade-weighted basket \par stood at 99.16, indicating the yuan depreciated by 0.13 percent\par last week.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to check the yuan's recent\par depreciation has seen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves drop\par sharply, but PBOC vice-governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Yi Gang\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Monday that\par reserves remained stable. \par     China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves declined by $99.5 billion in January\par to $3.23 trillion after a record fall the previous month, with a\par Reuters poll showing it is likely to fell for a fourth straight\par month in February, easing to $3.2 trillion. The data could be\par released on Monday. \par     Addressing the issue of the slowdown of China's economy,\par which has been the main factor behind the yuan depreciation\par expectations, the country's top economic planner said on Sunday\par that the economy is not headed for a hard landing.\par  \par     The offshore yuan was trading 0.12 percent firmer\par than the onshore spot at 6.507 per dollar. \par     The onshore yuan strengthened 0.2 percent against the euro\par  by midday at 7.1566. It also firmed 0.2 percent\par against the Japanese yen, hovering at 5.7316 to\par 100 yen.\par \par     The yuan market at a glance: \par     \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  PBOC midpoint      6.5113   6.5284    0.26%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.5149   6.5066    -0.13%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    0.06%              \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change YTD                       -0.33%\par  Spot change since 2005                27.04%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET    \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.507     0.12%\par         *                        \par  Offshore              6.7075    -2.93%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par \par     \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Kim Coghill)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-3-7T06:35:14.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160307ec3700bnh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\png