\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW- \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  should avoid  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2 , capital controls-ex-IMF official\b0\par\par\uc2 512 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2016\par 10:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not resort to capital controls or \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter yuan depreciation, as capital outflows are merely a symptom of structural problems that need to be addressed as its economy slows, a former senior \uc2 IMF\uc2  official said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell nearly $100 billion in January after a record $107.9 billion decline in December as its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to sell dollars to defend the yuan and staunch capital outflows.\par \par \uc2 They likely fell for a fourth straight month in February, though by a smaller amount than in previous months, according to a Reuters poll.\par \par \uc2 While that would still likely leave China's reserves at well over $3 trillion, financial markets are growing concerned that it has been burning through them at such a pace that Beijing might soon have to allow a sharp fall in the yuan or back-pedal on liberalisation and tighten capital controls.\par \par \uc2 Anne Krueger, a prominent academic who served as the International Monetary Fund's deputy managing director from 2001 to 2006, said outflows of around $100 billion per month were sustainable as China has plenty of reserves for the time being.\par \par \uc2 She said it would be counter-productive for authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prevent the yuan from depreciating.\par \par \uc2 "I doubt that's a good solution. That tells everybody that the authorities think there will be continued depreciation. That gives people all the more motive to try to get the money out," Krueger told Reuters in an interview on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Letting the yuan depreciate is one way to offset some of the problems China faces as its economy slows and suffers from excess capacity.\par \par \uc2 "The capital outflow is a symptom of the underlying problems they have to face, not in itself the problem," she said.\par \par \uc2 "When there are strong market forces for (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) depreciation, fighting these forces is a losing battle almost always," said Krueger, a professor at Johns Hopkins University who was visiting Tokyo to attend an \uc2 IMF\uc2 -hosted seminar.\par \par \uc2 Some policymakers, including Bank of Japan Governor Haruhiko Kuroda, have said imposing capital controls could be one step China could take to stave off a disruptive capital flight.\par \par \uc2 Krueger, however, said imposing capital controls would have high costs as it would "confirm to everybody who wants to get their money out that they were right."\par \par \uc2 "Imposing more capital controls at this stage would be the wrong answer," she said, urging Beijing to focus on tackling structural problems such as excess capacity and a rigid labour market.\par \par \uc2 China has roiled global markets twice in six months with surprise moves in the yuan, first with a surprise devaluation last August and again when it allowed a sharp slide in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar in early January.\par \par \uc2 In both cases the moves triggered unexpectedly heavy yuan selling, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  quickly and forcefully to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting by Leika Kihara; Editing by Kim Coghill)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-3-7T09:06:01.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160304ec3400pxd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
