\par\par \b \uc2 Offshore Chinese yuan up sharply as Chinese leaders convene in Beijing\b0\par\par\uc2 662 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2016\par 09:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI/HONG KONG, March 4 (Reuters) - The offshore yuan\par  rose more sharply against the dollar than its onshore\par counterpart on Friday, as Chinese leaders met in the capital to\par ratify development plans for the next five years.\par     The offshore Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose a sharper 0.8\par percent against the dollar while onshore yuan was up\par 0.2 percent from Thursday's close, falling back from a nearly\par 0.4 percent gain earlier in the day.\par     The Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  - both in the onshore market and in\par Hong Kong - had sold off sharply in December and January as\par markets fretted that Chinese policymakers had lost control of\par depreciation expectations amid strong capital outflows.\par     But with China's leadership currently meeting to approve the\par country's economic development blueprint for the next five years\par in Beijing this week, analysts say state banks have been\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sharply to ensure the yuan performs well.\par     "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hopes to keep the yuan steady and dampen\par yuan depreciation expectations during the (National People's\par Congress)," said Kenix Lai, senior market analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of\par East Asia\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Hong Kong, adding that both the offshore and\par onshore yuan are up simultaneously partly due to the weakness of\par the dollar, but mainly because of state bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par behalf of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in both markets.\par     Traders also cited strong foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sales by state\par banks in the morning session.\par     "Recently state banks like Agricultural Bank of China and\par ICBC (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Industrial and Commercial Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) have been\par constantly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to support the\par yuan," said a dealer at a Chinese commercial bank in Shanghai.\par     The offshore yuan was also trading largely below the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's midpoint for the onshore market for two sessions in a\par row, a rarity.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the onshore yuan midpoint rate at\par 6.5284 per dollar prior to market open, 0.20 percent firmer than\par the previous fix 6.5412, reflecting the dollar's weakness in\par global markets.\par     China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has now strengthened against the dollar for\par four straight sessions, following the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's surprise\par move to cut bank reserve ratio requirements on Feb. 29.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials had previously stated that they were\par reluctant to cut reserve ratios while capital flows remained\par strong, as such cuts release large amounts of cash into the\par banking system which could pressure the exchange rate.\par  \par     Following the surprise cut, economists speculated that the\par apparent about-face might mean that capital outflows had begun\par to slow following a raft of stricter monitoring measures by\par Chinese regulators. \par     Despite the yuan's steadiness in the past week, a Reuters\par poll suggests the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  faces further depreciation pressure\par due to the uncertainties surrounding the health of the world's\par second-largest economy. \par     The yuan is expected to weaken some 3.5 percent against the\par U.S. dollar over the coming year, but analysts also said they do\par not expect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to sharply devalue the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par coming months. \par \par     ONSHORE:\par  Item               Current  Previous  Change\par  PBOC midpoint      6.5284   6.5412    0.20%\par                                        \par  Spot yuan          6.523    6.5351    0.19%\par                                        \par  Divergence from    -0.08%             \par  midpoint*                             \par  Spot change YTD                       -0.45%\par  Spot change since 2005                26.88%\par  revaluation                           \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par   \par  Instrument            Current   Difference\par                                  from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan    6.5167    0.10%\par         *                        \par  Offshore              6.725     -2.92%\par  non-deliverable                 \par  forwards                        \par                **                \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par \par     \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom, Nathaniel Taplin and\par Michelle Chen in HONG KONG; Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-3-4T09:33:30.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160304ec3400nrm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
