\par\par \b \uc2 European Morning Briefing: Stocks Seen Boosted by Sharp Oil Gains\b0\par\par\uc2 3,728 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2016\par 05:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Snapshot: \par ======== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stocks rally to continue; EUR/USD 1.1166; bonds seen weaker; Brent crude $34.59; gold $1193.62\f28 \par \par \uc2 -Saudi, Russian Oil Ministers Head to Qatar to Discuss Production\par \par \uc2 -German Finance Minister Says Market Volatility Is Affecting Economic Conditions\par \par \uc2 -Japan Finance Minister: Additional Fiscal Stimulus Not on Table\par \par \uc2 -Japan Prime Minister Abe Adviser Hamada Says Finance Ministry Should \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market\par \par \uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  Jan New Yuan Loans Hit Monthly Record High\par \par \uc2 -Liberty Global Plans Netherlands Joint Venture With \uc2 Vodafone\par \par \uc2 -Daimler to Lay Off More Than 1,200 at North Carolina Truck Plants\par \par \uc2 -VW Memo Warned of Emission Issues in 2014\par \par \uc2 -Anglo American Credit Rating Downgraded to Junk\par \par \uc2 Watch For: German ZEW Business Survey; U.K. inflation; earnings from \uc2 Anglo American\uc2 , Orange, \uc2 TNT Express\uc2 , \uc2 Air Liquide\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Headline News: \par ============= \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wolfgang Sch\u228\'00\'E4uble\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday that recent volatility in financial markets is affecting global economic conditions and financial officials from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Group of 20\f28 \uc2 \f2  nations will discuss how to deal with the current uncertainties.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We have an economic situation that's marked by a wide range of volatility, crises and uncertainties which we have rarely faced before to this extent," he said at a conference organized by Germany's real estate sector.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He said finance ministers and central bankers from the G-20 countries will discuss the situation at their meeting in Shanghai, China, next week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Taro Aso said Tuesday that he isn't considering any additional fiscal stimulus measures, playing down economic weakness over the winter months as a phenomenon caused by unusually warm weather.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We are not thinking about additional measures at this stage," Mr. Aso said at a news conference following a regular meeting of government ministers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Aso said the relatively warm weather had "quite a big impact" on economic activity during the October-December quarter, in which the economy shrank for the second time in three quarters.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An adviser to Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shinzo Abe\f28 \uc2 \f2  said that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  should \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to curb volatility in the yen, saying the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rebound since last week is unusually sharp.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The yen's recent appreciation is abnormal from statistical perspectives" and appears driven by hedge funds, said Koichi Hamada, one of Mr. Abe's close economic advisers and a Yale University professor emeritus, in a recent interview with The Wall Street Journal.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Accordingly, I think the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the markets, not to guide the yen in any particular direction but to prevent high volatility by sending a warning to speculators."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese financial institutions issued 2.51 trillion yuan ($385.5 billion) worth of new yuan loans in January, the highest monthly level on record, data from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  showed Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The new credit figure was up significantly from the 597.8 billion yuan recorded in December and was also above the 1.9 trillion yuan forecast by The Wall Street Journal's poll of 13 economists. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Shares: \par ====== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rally in European stocks looks likely to continue Tuesday with IG calling the DAX up 56 points at 9262, the CAC up 20 at 4135 and the FTSE up 26 at 5850.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's shares rallied Tuesday, leading gains across Asia as signs of stability emerged in the Chinese yuan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Shanghai Composite Index was last up 2.8%, extending gains from the open. The Nikkei Stock Average was up 0.9% and the S&P \f28 \uc2 \f2 ASX\f28 \uc2 \f2  200 edged up 0.1%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. stock markets were closed Monday for the Presidents' Day holiday but futures suggest opening gains of around 1.7% for the Dow and S&P when trading resumes later. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Corporate News: \par ============== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S.-based cable operator Liberty Global said Monday it is setting up a joint venture combining its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the Netherlands with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vodafone\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vodafone\f28 \uc2 \f2  will pay \f28 \uc2 \f2 Liberty Global\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the Europe-focused operator controlled by cable tycoon \f28 \uc2 \f2 John Malone\f28 \uc2 \f2 , 1 billion euros ($1.12 billion) as part of the deal, according to a statement. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Liberty\f28 \uc2 \f2  said after integration costs, the 50-50 joint venture would be worth about 3.5 billion euros in terms of combined revenue and capital expenditures.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The tie-up would merge \f28 \uc2 \f2 Liberty Global\f28 \uc2 \f2 's cable and Internet businesses with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vodafone\f28 \uc2 \f2 's mobile \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to create a Netherlands-wide communications provider with more than 15 million subscribers, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Liberty Global\f28 \uc2 \f2  said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Daimler said it would lay off more than 1,200 workers this week at a pair of North Carolina assembly plants in response to falling demand for commercial trucks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Daimler's North America truck unit, which makes Freightliner trucks, said Monday it plans to furlough 550 workers at its Cleveland assembly plant, a quarter of the plant's employees. More than one-third of the workforce at Daimler's Mount Holly plant, about 700 employees in all, will be laid off as well. The layoffs will take effect Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A senior \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen\f28 \uc2 \f2  executive commissioned with troubleshooting and known internally as "the fireman" warned the company's top management in May 2014 about an impending investigation by U.S. environmental authorities into whether the German car maker was using "test recognition" on some of its diesel engines.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The warning, communicated in a note to then-Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Martin Winterkorn\f28 \uc2 \f2 , came from Bernd Gottweis, a quality-control executive who ran a team of product sleuths that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen\f28 \uc2 \f2  management dispatched around the world to put out quality flare-ups before they grew into a full-fledged blaze.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The memo makes the first known reference to a defeat device in the investigation into \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen\f28 \uc2 \f2 's emissions-cheating scandal and might suggest that the company's top executives knew more than they are saying now. It isn't known whether Mr. Winterkorn saw the memo. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par ===== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The EUR/USD pair has lost its bullish technical stance on the daily chart, and could therefore slip lower due to capitulation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EUR/USD came under strong selling pressure in the U.S., after European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mario Draghi\f28 \uc2 \f2  sent a dovish message to the market. The reiteration of \f28 \uc2 \f2 the ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2 's willingness to further loosen monetary policy, possibly as soon as next month, in order to achieve inflation targets sent the euro tumbling. EUR/USD could be on its way even lower, now that it has dropped out of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel--which acts as a chart resistance at 1.1222.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The pair might be headed for the 1.1043 chart support next, which is the 20-day Bollinger mid line. A break of this barrier could pave the way for further euro weakness. At 0123 GMT, EUR/USD was 1.1166 from its Monday close of 1.1153.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After a 1.3% rally for the yuan Monday, \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has dampened expectations for more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation. The daily USD/CNY benchmark rate was set higher Tuesday at 6.5130 versus Monday's 6.5118, implying a marginal weakening of the yuan against the dollar. The adjustment likely factored in Monday's dollar index rally. The elevated fixing may motivate short-covering in the USD/CNY spot market. At 0142 GMT, USD/CNY was 6.5040 from its Monday close of 6.4940. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Bonds: \par ===== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European government bonds are likely to remain under pressure with the rally in equities set to continue.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. bond markets were closed on Monday so investors will struggle for fresh cues, although \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mario Draghi\f28 \uc2 \f2 's commitment to boost stimulus, if necessary, could weigh further on sentiment. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Energy: \par ====== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The energy ministers of Saudi Arabia and Russia--the world's two largest crude-oil exporters--are set to discuss production in Qatar on Tuesday, \f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  delegates said Monday, amid mounting pressure to prop up fallen oil prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The meeting between Saudi Arabia's Ali al-Naimi and Russia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alexander Novak\f28 \uc2 \f2  comes after Iran launched its first oil exports to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  in over three years, following the lifting of sanctions over its nuclear program. Iranian officials said over the weekend that the country had boosted exports by 400,000 barrels a day, adding to an already saturated global oil market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials say a new idea has been discussed in recent days--a production "freeze," requiring members and Russia to not pump more than they are now. That would allow Iran to continue pumping at its current rate, while Russia wouldn't have to change much as its production is projected to be flat this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude-oil prices rose in early Asia trade on the news. On the \f28 \uc2 \f2 New York Mercantile Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 , light, sweet crude futures for delivery in March traded at $30.82 a barrel at 0330 GMT, up $1.38 in the Globex electronic session. April Brent crude on London's \f28 \uc2 \f2 ICE\f28 \uc2 \f2  Futures exchange rose $1.20 to $34.59 a barrel.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Saudi Arabia is not eager to cut production to restore the supply and demand balance, but could consider output cuts if other producers join," ANZ Research said in a note. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Metals: \par ====== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spot gold prices fell below $1,200 per ounce in Asia, erasing recent gains from greater safe-haven demand due to volatility in other financial assets.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A rebound in risk assets such as equities suppressed gold's demand. At 0359 GMT, spot gold was at $1,193.62 per troy ounce.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to paul.larkins@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 15 Feb 2016 23:35 ET \par European Morning Briefing: DJ Exclusive Headlines; Other Top Stories\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DJ Exclusive Headlines:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Apollo Global Management\f28 \uc2 \f2  Nears Acquisition Deal for ADT\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/apollo-global-management-nears-acquisition-deal-for-adt-1455584149"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/apollo-global-management-nears-acquisition-deal-for-adt-1455584149}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan Prime Minister Abe Adviser Hamada Says Finance Ministry Should \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Market\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/abes-adviser-says-finance-ministry-should-intervene-in-currency-market-1455587564"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/abes-adviser-says-finance-ministry-should-\b  \highlight22intervene\b0 \highlight22 -in-\b  \highlight22currency\b0 \highlight22 -market-1455587564}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil Nearing Deal With Mining Companies Over Dam Collapse\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/brazil-nearing-deal-with-mining-companies-over-dam-collapse-1455579135"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/brazil-nearing-deal-with-mining-companies-over-dam-collapse-1455579135}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 GE's Oil and Gas Chief Explores Opportunities in Iran\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/ges-oil-and-gas-chief-explores-opportunities-in-iran-1455577402"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/ges-oil-and-gas-chief-explores-opportunities-in-iran-1455577402}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Other Top Stories:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Saudi, Russian Oil Ministers Head to Qatar to Discuss Production\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The energy ministers of Saudi Arabia and Russia-the world's two largest crude-oil exporters-are set to discuss production in Qatar on Tuesday, \f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  delegates said Monday, amid mounting pressure to prop up fallen oil prices.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/saudi-russian-oil-ministers-head-to-qatar-to-discuss-production-1455566388"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/saudi-russian-oil-ministers-head-to-qatar-to-discuss-production-1455566388}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 German Finance Minister Says Market Volatility Is Affecting Economic Conditions\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wolfgang Sch\u228\'00\'E4uble\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday that recent volatility in financial markets is affecting global economic conditions and financial officials from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Group of 20\f28 \uc2 \f2  nations will discuss how to deal with the current uncertainties.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/german-finance-minister-says-market-volatility-is-affecting-economic-conditions-1455566382"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/german-finance-minister-says-market-volatility-is-affecting-economic-conditions-1455566382}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan Finance Minister: Additional Fiscal Stimulus Not on Table\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Taro Aso said Tuesday that he isn't considering any additional fiscal stimulus measures, playing down economic weakness over the winter months as a phenomenon caused by unusually warm weather.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/japan-finance-minister-additional-fiscal-stimulus-not-on-table-1455588982"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/japan-finance-minister-additional-fiscal-stimulus-not-on-table-1455588982}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 China Premier Vows to Guard Against Financial Risks\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Premier \f28 \uc2 \f2 Li Keqiang\f28 \uc2 \f2  pledged to step up efforts to stay vigilant against risks in the financial market, while reiterating that the country's economic fundamentals remain solid due to steady employment.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/china-premier-vows-to-guard-against-financial-risks-1455593183"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/china-premier-vows-to-guard-against-financial-risks-1455593183}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 China Jan New Yuan Loans Hit Monthly Record High\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese financial institutions issued 2.51 trillion yuan ($385.5 billion) worth of new yuan loans in January, the highest monthly level on record, data from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  showed Tuesday.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/china-jan-new-yuan-loans-hit-monthly-record-high-1455592511"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/china-jan-new-yuan-loans-hit-monthly-record-high-1455592511}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Liberty Global Plans Netherlands Joint Venture With \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vodafone\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S.-based cable operator Liberty Global PLC said Monday it is setting up a joint venture combining its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the Netherlands with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vodafone Group PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/liberty-global-plans-netherlands-joint-venture-with-vodafone-1455590304"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/liberty-global-plans-netherlands-joint-venture-with-vodafone-1455590304}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Daimler to Lay Off More Than 1,200 at North Carolina Truck Plants\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Daimler AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it would lay off more than 1,200 workers this week at a pair of North Carolina assembly plants in response to falling demand for commercial trucks.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/daimler-to-lay-off-more-than-1-200-at-north-carolina-truck-plants-1455584141"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/daimler-to-lay-off-more-than-1-200-at-north-carolina-truck-plants-1455584141}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 VW Memo Warned of Emission Issues in 2014\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A senior \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  executive commissioned with troubleshooting and known internally as "the fireman" warned the company's top management in May 2014 about an impending investigation by U.S. environmental authorities into whether the German car maker was using "test recognition" on some of its diesel engines.\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/vw-memo-warned-of-emission-issues-in-2014-1455572391"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/vw-memo-warned-of-emission-issues-in-2014-1455572391}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 15 Feb 2016 23:35 ET \par European Morning Briefing: Market Prices and G7 Calendar\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par DJIA      Closed \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nasdaq\f28 \uc2 \f2     Closed \par S&P 500   Closed \par FTSE 100  5824.28 116.68 2.04% \par Xetra DAX 9206.84 239.33 2.67% \par CAC40     4115.25 120.19 3.01% \par Closing \par  \par Futures: \par Dow      16195.00 282.00 1.77% \par S&P 500   1892.25  34.00 1.83% \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nasdaq\f28 \uc2 \f2     4097.75  91.50 2.28% \par As of 0358 GMT \par  \par Nikkei    16264.85 242.27 1.51% \par Shanghai   2823.86  77.66 2.83% \par Hang Seng 19228.55 310.41 1.64% \par S&P/ASX    4880.50  37.00 0.76% \par Kospi      1891.16  28.96 1.56% \par Taipei     8190.41 123.90 1.54% \par As of 0425 GMT \par  \par USD/JPY 114.79-80 0.17% \par Range 114.85-114.29 \par EUR/USD 1.1157-60 0.04% \par Range 1.1185-1.1153 \par GBP/USD 1.4430-32 -0.03% \par Range 1.4457-1.4430 \par USD/CHF 0.9875-