\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan Makes Biggest Jump Since 2005 on PBOC Cue\b0\par\par\uc2 688 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Februar 2016\par 07:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit its strongest level this year after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday guided it sharply upward against a tide of stumbling global financial markets.\par \par \uc2 After opening stronger against the dollar, the yuan traded as much as 1.35% higher than the previous close, its biggest gain since 2005, the year the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peg to the dollar ended. The yuan strengthened to 6.4880 against the dollar and last traded at 6.4938.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the yuan almost 1% stronger, at 6.5118, than where it had closed against the dollar on Feb. 5, making it the strongest daily reference rate since Jan. 4. Chinese markets were closed last week for the Lunar New Year holiday.\par \par \uc2 The yuan is allowed to trade 2% above or below the daily reference rate against the dollar, which is set by \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . After vowing in August to make the rate more market-driven, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent months has sought to guide investors away from it and toward a new exchange-rate index linked to a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On Feb. 5, the China \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trade System, or CFETS, index fell to its lowest level since the end of 2014.\par \par \uc2 In a note to clients Monday, analysts from Scotiabank wrote that "the daily reference rate will not be completely determined by the market given its marked spillover effects," saying that "a string of surging [yuan] fixings could fuel market fears over competitive devaluation."\par \par \uc2 After depreciating 1.5% in the first week of the year, the yuan has since risen 1.5%.\par \par \uc2 The freely traded offshore yuan continued to strengthen, rising as much as 0.4% against the dollar Monday to its strongest level since early December.\par \par \uc2 Monday's moves closed the gap between the yuan's onshore and offshore rates, which has been a headache for Beijing after it widened to more than 2% earlier this year. Traders cited the possibility of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trade.\par \par \uc2 Stocks in mainland \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell on the first trading day after the holiday, catching up to losses in markets around the world last week. The Shanghai Composite Index ended down 0.6% after falling nearly 3% intraday. China's imports and exports continued to deteriorate in January, data released Monday showed.\par \par \uc2 As markets globally have struggled to find a firm footing in the past few weeks, investors have fled to haven assets including the Japanese yen, sending the dollar sharply weaker since early February. Data from the \uc2 U.S. Commodity Futures Trading Commission\uc2  showed that investors last week cut their bets on the dollar by $3 billion for the second consecutive week. This was the lowest level since October 2014, when the dollar's rally began to show signs of petering out.\par \par \uc2 Widely cited comments by the People's Bank of China Governor \uc2 Zhou Xiaochuan\uc2  over the weekend in local media "signal against the intention for a sharp one-off devaluation, but leave scope for possible further round(s) of gradual depreciation," analysts from \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  wrote in a note to clients Monday.\par \par \uc2 In the interview posted on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's website, Mr. Zhou said "in the mind of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there is not an optimal, model-produced exchange rate level," adding that "as the next step we will strengthen the reference to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 He also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has "always held the view that the efficient market hypothesis cannot be relied on 100%," referring to a theory that states market prices fully reflect all relevant information, and there is no way to beat the market.\par \par \uc2 In a statement published on the CFETS website on Feb. 3, the regulator reiterated its intention to guide its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  alongside the basket, noting that "with the improvement of the market-oriented exchange rate regime, [yuan] exchange rate will continue referring to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and enhancing its flexibility. "\par \par \uc2 Write to Anjani Trivedi at anjani.trivedi@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 15, 2016 01:25 ET (06:25 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160215ec2f000db\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
