\par\par \b \uc2 China Yuan Moves May Slow Group Seeking Greater Ties\b0\par\par\uc2 583 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2016\par 08:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par C4\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    (FROM THE WALL STREET JOURNAL 1/26/16) \par    By Margot Patrick \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Efforts by a group of U.S. heavyweights to foster closer ties to Chinese markets could be hampered by China's moves to control its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 As China kept markets guessing last week on the yuan's next move and future \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Working Group on U.S. RMB Trading and Clearing met for the first time in New York last Wednesday to look atways to encourage more yuan trading and clearing in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Led by former New York Mayor \uc2 Michael Bloomberg\uc2  as chairman, and with co-chairmen that include former Treasury secretaries \uc2 Timothy Geithner\uc2  and \uc2 Henry Paulson\uc2 , the meeting marked a new turn in China-U.S. financial cooperation and followed a September agreement by President \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  and President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  to facilitate usage of the yuan in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Not on the group's agenda last week, but a pressing concern for many banks and companies doing yuan business, is what further controls China might put in place to stabilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . After years of being seen as a one-way upward bet against the dollar, the yuan has weakened sharply since last year, leading to heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Analysts predict China will take a pause on its longer-term plans to loosen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls, putting the future of offshore yuan business in doubt.\par \par \uc2 "Given persistent large capital outflows, we expect to see a slowdown in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market liberalization and tight enforcement of existing capital controls in the near term," analysts at \uc2 Standard Chartered PLC\uc2  said in a note last week. Recent measures by China suggest "that capital account opening and renminbi internationalization will take a breather," they said. Renminbi, often shortened to RMB, is another word for yuan.\par \par \uc2 Much of the action this month by Chinese authorities centered around the offshore yuan, which trades freely outside China, in contrast to the tightly controlled onshore yuan rate set daily by the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 . Foreign banks trading offshore yuan were ordered to start placing reserves with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and some were forced to temporarily suspend some trading activities.\par \par \uc2 At Wednesday's meeting, Mr. Bloomberg said the recent volatility in China, and the global market reaction, "shows how interconnected the U.S. and Chinese economies are."\par \par \uc2 "That makes the work of this group even more important," Mr. Bloomberg said.\par \par \uc2 The meeting, at \uc2 Bloomberg LP\uc2 's headquarters, came days before reports that Mr. Bloomberg is considering entering this year's presidential race. The group was set up in November to follow in the footsteps of financial centers such as Hong Kong and London in helping to internationalize the yuan.\par \par \uc2 Members, including big American and Chinese banks such as \uc2 J.P. Morgan Chase & Co\uc2 , \uc2 Citigroup Inc\uc2 . and Bank of China, formed four work streams at the meeting. They will consider operating models, identify regulatory issues, look at possible yuan products and services and assess market demand.\par \par \uc2 The plan is to submit a possible road map to U.S. authorities that will make it easier for U.S. firms to transact in yuan. Mr. Bloomberg said trading and clearing yuan in the U.S. "will lower transaction costs, increase efficiency, and help build stronger trade and business partnerships -- all of which creates jobs and spurs economic growth."\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 26, 2016 02:34 ET (07:34 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160126ec1q000nr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
