\par\par \b \uc2 CNH TRACKER-Restrictive measures cast shadow over yuan globalisation\b0\par\par\uc2 684 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2016\par 08:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Jan 21 (Reuters) - The Chinese yuan's accelerating internationalisation lost some of its shine after Beijing launched a batch of restrictive measures over recent weeks to control cross-border flows and squeeze out speculators.               \par \par \uc2 These control measures, seen as a setback to Beijing's efforts to open up its domestic market and liberalise the capital account, may affect investor faith in China's policies and the internationalisation process itself, analysts say.               \par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it will start implementing a reserve requirement ratio (RRR) on offshore banks' domestic yuan deposits to help set up a long-term mechanism to regulate fund flows.               \par \par \uc2 In addition, regulators are imposing limits on cross-border flows from yuan-denominated capital pools and requiring intensified checks on related transactions, people with direct knowledge of the new measures told Reuters.               \par \par \uc2 These measures followed frequent suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by   the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  in both onshore and offshore yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets earlier this month to stabilise its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and shake out speculative funds betting on yuan depreciation.               \par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 PBOC\uc2 's heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  these days would undo some achieved progress in offshore market development... It may remind the policymaker to rethink about the strategy for RMB internationalization," \uc2 China International Capital Corporation\uc2  (CICC) analysts said in a report.               \par \par \uc2 China rolled out a series of new policies last year to facilitate cross-border fund flows more quickly than the market had expected, but the yuan's quick depreciation and flourishing arbitrage have brought the deregulatory drive to a sharp halt.               \par \par \uc2 "The yuan's internationalisation process is set to slow down and faces challenges as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to fall further, which is a fundamental change from several years ago," said an executive at a Chinese brokerage in Hong Kong.               \par \par \uc2 It was difficult to promote yuan-denominated investment products to foreign investors under such circumstances because \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses would eat into their returns, the executive said.               \par \par \uc2 Indeed, the dim sum bond market - which helped pioneer the yuan's internationalisation - has lost steam and is expected to see even fewer issues this year as investors gradually switch back to U.S. dollar assets.               \par \par \uc2 The yuan has lost 4 percent against the dollar in the past three months. \uc2 BMI Research\uc2  on Tuesday revised down its forecast for the yuan to 7.1 per dollar by the end of this year from 6.8 previously.                                             \par \par \uc2 WEEK IN REVIEW:               \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Hong Kong Exchanges and Clearing\uc2  will launch new initiatives including an onshore China commodities platform and a way for foreign companies to list via the Hong Kong-Shanghai Stock Connect program, HKEx Chief Executive Charles Li said on Thursday.               \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Taiwan's Financial Supervisory Commission\uc2  (FSC) will require banks to set aside reserves for possible default of a yuan derivative products amid sharp falls in the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , three sources close to the regulator said on Monday.               \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and commercial banks sold a net 629 billion yuan ($95.61 billion) worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  in December, data showed on Monday, or nearly triple the figure of the previous month, as capital outflows grew.               \par \par \uc2 * China's economic growth in the fourth quarter slowed to the weakest since the financial crisis, adding pressure on a government that is struggling to restore the confidence of investors after perceived policy missteps jolted global markets.               \par \par \uc2 * India would be very concerned if China were to allow a major devaluation in the yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , its \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  summit negotiator told Reuters, adding that he doubted Beijing would allow this to happen.                                             \par \par \uc2 CHART OF THE WEEK:               \par \par \uc2 China GDP and exports: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/zeq95s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/zeq95s}}}\par \par \uc2 RECENT STORIES: Dim sum bond sale commissions shrink, volume halves in 2015   Big fall in HK dollar as offshore yuan buckles, but peg safe   Banks give back China investment quotas as clients bypass the middlemen                              \par \par \uc2 More stories about the CNH market   Daily onshore yuan reports   Daily China money market reports   Offshore yuan rate    Onshore yuan rate   Offshore yuan dealt  Onshore yuan on CFETS     \uc2 THOMSON REUTERS\uc2  SPEED GUIDES                              \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-1-21T08:07:28.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160121ec1l007q1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
