\par\par \b \uc2 European Morning Briefing: Market Fear Back as China, Oil Panic Grow\b0\par\par\uc2 3,666 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2016\par 05:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Snapshot: \par ======== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stocks to slide; EUR/USD 1.0890; bonds seen in demand; Brent crude at $39.94; gold at $1093.00\f28 \par \par \uc2 -China's Yuan Falls Sharply Offshore\par \par \uc2 -BOJ Gov Kuroda Again Stresses Readiness to Act\par \par \uc2 -Japanese Machinery Orders Fall Sharply in November\par \par \uc2 -China \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Regulator Says No New Limit Imposed on Dollar Buying\par \par \uc2 -Fed's Evans Calls for 'Very Gradual Policy Normalization\par \par \uc2 -\uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  , \uc2 EPA\uc2  Fail to Break Impasse in Emissions-Cheating Scandal\par \par \uc2 -Porsche CEO Sees Stable Operating Profit in the Next Few Years\par \par \uc2 -Libya Meets With Energy Companies to Bolster Recovery of Its Damaged Petroleum Sector\par \par \uc2 Watch For: \uc2 World Economic Forum\uc2  's Global Risk Report; Germany GDP; Italy industrial production; \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  rate decision; speeches by \uc2 IMF\uc2  's Lagarde, Fed's Bullard; earnings from \uc2 J.P. Morgan Chase\uc2  , \uc2 Intel\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Headline News: \par ============= \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Haruhiko Kuroda reiterated Thursday that he is prepared to take "bolder action" if necessary to achieve the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's inflation goal, continuing his efforts to dispel a perception that the bank may be out of ammunition or hesitant to move.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We will do everything we can to achieve 2% inflation no matter what," Mr. Kuroda said at a New Year meeting hosted by regional Japanese banks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite his bullish remarks about the bank's readiness to step up action if necessary, Mr. Kuroda also said at the meeting that Japan's underlying inflation has continued to "steadily improve."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese core machinery orders fell sharply for the first drop in three months in November, the government said Thursday, as sluggish global growth weighs on Japanese business sentiment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Core orders, a leading indicator of business investment, fell 14.4% on month after seasonal adjustment. Economists surveyed by The Wall Street Journal and the Nikkei had expected a decline of 7.8%. On a year-on-year basis, orders rose 1.2%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulator said Wednesday that it didn't impose any new limit on individuals' purchases of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 State Administration of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on its official Weibo account that it didn't limit or require reservations for individuals' purchases of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the nation's commercial banks.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some media reported that retail investors in China have lately been making reservations for purchases of over $5,000, which doesn't conform to current rules, the regulator said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Stocks: \par ====== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The recent rebound in European stocks is likely to abruptly end Thursday as investor anxiety returns.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ahead of the open, IG has called the DAX down 168 points at 9792, the CAC down 79 at 4312 and the FTSE down 104 at 5856.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China shares flirted with bear-market territory in a volatile session Thursday that deepened losses across the region.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Shanghai Composite Index breached its lows from last summer's crash, after falling as much as 2.8%. The benchmark was last down 1.2% at 2914.37.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The current level puts the index on track to enter a bear market, defined as a fall of 20% or more from its recent high, reached on Dec. 22. China's main stock benchmark is off 44% from its June peak and down 7% year-to-date.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere in Asia, markets were down sharply. Losses in the mining sector and a strengthening yen drove Japan's Nikkei Stock Average down 3.7%. Australia's S&P/ASX 200 was down 1.5% and Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index fell 1.6%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A broad selloff in stocks accelerated Wednesday, dragging the Dow Jones Industrial Average to its lowest level since late September.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Dow fell 2.2%, the S&P 500 dropped 2.5% and the Nasdaq Composite declined 3.4%. The S&P 500 entered correction territory, as defined by a 10% decline from a recent high. The Nasdaq Composite entered a correction Monday. The Dow is down 9.9% from its recent high in November.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "You look across the spectrum, and there's been nowhere to really go and hide," said Sahak Manuelian, managing director in equity trading at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wedbush Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Corporate News: \par ============== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen\f28 \uc2 \f2  and U.S. environmental officials failed Wednesday to announce a breakthrough in talks between the company's CEO and the head of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Environmental Protection Agency\f28 \uc2 \f2  , casting doubt over a quick resolution of the German auto maker's emissions-cheating scandal after months of negotiations with U.S. officials.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In curt, nearly identical statements, Volkswagen Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Matthias M\u252\'00\'FCller\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Gina McCarthy, head of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EPA\f28 \uc2 \f2  , thanked each other for taking time to meet and pledged to keep talking. The parties gave no indication they made any progress during an hourlong meeting at \f28 \uc2 \f2 EPA\f28 \uc2 \f2  offices in Washington, D.C.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Porsche chief executive Oliver Blume said he expects operating profit in the next few years to remain stable at around the level of the past two years, given high investments, speaking in an interview on the sidelines of the North American International Auto Show in Detroit. For 2016, Mr. Blume expects sales growth in deliveries in at least a single-digit-percentage range. \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : \par ===== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's yuan fell sharply in early trade in the offshore market Thursday, cutting into some of the gains the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  made earlier this week when the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up its value.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It fell as much as 0.64% to 6.6071 in the offshore market even after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the rate at which it trades in the domestic market stronger against the U.S. dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The [Chinese] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is causing tension in the whole world," said Stephen Ma, head of greater China at BMO Global Asset Management. "What we're seeing now is the result of a lot of government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earlier, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixed the yuan at 6.5616 to one U.S. dollar, slightly stronger from the previous fix of 6.5630 on Wednesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The onshore yuan, which can trade 2% above or below the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's daily guidance, was last at 6.5861, slightly weaker than 6.5756 the previous session.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Tuesday, the cost of borrowing yuan overnight in the offshore market surged to as high as 66.815% but fell the following day and was close to 4% in the market by early Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro edged slightly higher in Asia, adding to its bounce from a week-low that was triggered by a fresh bout of risk aversion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In recent weeks, the euro has been trading with a new dynamic - it rallies when risk appetite is poor, due to the funding-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  characteristics of the EUR/USD pair. Increasingly risk-averse market participants fled to the safety of U.S. Treasurys and gold. Further unwinding of risk-on positions would entail covering short-EUR/USD positions, and buying of USD/Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The short EUR/Asia fundamental trade idea was highly popular among macro hedge funds in 2015.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 0044 GMT, EUR/USD was 1.0890 from its Wednesday close of 1.0873. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Bonds: \par ===== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European bonds are likely to be in strong demand as investors flee into fixed income to escape a panic-driven selloff in equities.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors piled into \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  bonds to preserve capital Wednesday, driving down the yield on the benchmark 10-year note toward 2%, as a new round of large price declines in U.S. stocks heightened concerns over riskier assets and the global economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The flight for safety pushed down the yield on the 10-year note to 2.07%, compared with 2.1% on Tuesday. It was the yield's lowest closing level since Oct. 27--the month when the yield last traded below the 2% mark.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Treasurys are clearly in demand in this risk-off environment," said Justin Lederer, senior trader of interest rates at Cantor Fitzgerald in New York. "People are worried about China, oil, stocks...you name it." \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Energy: \par ====== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brent crude futures fell below $30 per barrel in Asia as concerns about Iran adding to a supply overhang in the short term continued to depress prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 February Brent crude on London's \f28 \uc2 \f2 ICE\f28 \uc2 \f2  Futures exchange was trading at $29.94/bbl, compared with the previous close at $30.31/bbl. On the \f28 \uc2 \f2 New York Mercantile Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  , light, sweet crude futures for delivery in February traded at $30.51/bbl, up 3 cents from the previous close.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The beginning of this year will certainly prove sloppier than we originally anticipated, but current prices are not sustainable in the medium term, and we continue to anticipate a recovery to the $50/bbl level near the end of this year," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBC Capital Markets\f28 \uc2 \f2  .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The head of Libya's state-oil company on Wednesday said he is meeting with major oil companies such as \f28 \uc2 \f2 BP\f28 \uc2 \f2  to try to jump-start the country's potential to produce petroleum, after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Islamic State\f28 \uc2 \f2  militants inflicted heavy damage to a key oil export terminal.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mustafa Sanallah, chairman of the state-run National Oil Co., said he is meeting France's Total, Italy's Eni and \f28 \uc2 \f2 BP\f28 \uc2 \f2  , among other companies in Istanbul, trying to convince them to resume exploration efforts in Libya, as a unity government is expected to take power this month. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Metals: \par ====== \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold prices regained ground in Asia after profit taking in the last couple of days checked a rally since the beginning of this year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Prices fell to as low as $1,080 per ounce Wednesday, after rallying past a psychological mark of $1,100/oz in the past week on safe haven demand following turbulence in stock markets and geo-political tensions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 0329 GMT, gold was at $1,093/oz, up from the previous close at $1,092.99/oz.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Paul Larkins at paul.larkins@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 13 Jan 2016 23:36 ET \par European Morning Briefing: DJ Exclusive Headlines; Other Top Stories\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DJ Exclusive Headlines:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Goldman Plans to Cut Up to 10% of Fixed-Income Traders, Salespeople\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/goldman-plans-to-cut-up-to-10-of-fixed-income-traders-salespeople-1452726472"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/goldman-plans-to-cut-up-to-10-of-fixed-income-traders-salespeople-1452726472 }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Tullow Revamps Business to Cope With Low Crude Prices\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/tullow-revamps-business-to-cope-with-low-crude-prices-1452715429"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/tullow-revamps-business-to-cope-with-low-crude-prices-1452715429 }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Libya Meets With Energy Companies to Bolster Recovery of Its Damaged Petroleum Sector\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/libya-meets-with-energy-companies-to-bolster-recovery-of-its-damaged-petroleum-sector-1452710819"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/libya-meets-with-energy-companies-to-bolster-recovery-of-its-damaged-petroleum-sector-1452710819 }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 Other Top Stories:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's Yuan Falls Sharply Offshore\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's yuan fell sharply in early trade in the offshore market Thursday, wiping out some of the gains made earlier this week when the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/chinas-yuan-falls-sharply-in-offshore-market-1452741919"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/chinas-yuan-falls-sharply-in-offshore-market-1452741919 }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 BOJ Gov Kuroda Again Stresses Readiness to Act\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Haruhiko Kuroda reiterated Thursday that he is prepared to take "bolder action" if necessary to achieve the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's inflation goal, continuing his efforts to dispel a perception that the bank may be out ammunition or hesitant to move.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Machinery Orders Fall Sharply in November\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese core machinery orders fell sharply for the first drop in three months in November, the government said Thursday, as sluggish global growth weighs on Japanese business sentiment\f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/japanese-machinery-orders-fall-sharply-in-november-1452744135"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/japanese-machinery-orders-fall-sharply-in-november-1452744135 }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 China \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Regulator Says No New Limit Imposed on Dollar Buying\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulator said Wednesday that it didn't impose any new limit on individuals' purchases of foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fed's Evans Calls for 'Very Gradual Policy Normalization\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago President \f28 \uc2 \f2 C